{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NbnPdkdKv5PyLu8mQUStHQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '部分假设未完全验证，需调整 claims 强度并补充实验。具体：(1) MPC/imagination 架构边界从 \"novel\n2\t  finding\" 弱化为 \"empirical observation consistent with architectural dependency\"，Discussion\n3\t  中加入 TAWM 设定差异的详细对比表（obs space / planning horizon / critic structure / dt range），明确哪些\n4\t  confounds 未控制；(2) 梯度-因果解耦从独立贡献降级为 C7 的 supporting analysis，不在 abstract/intro 中突出；(3)\n5\t  补充 ensemble critic 快速消融——在 DreamerV3 critic 上加 2-head ensemble + min-Q，即使简化版也堵住\n6\t  R9 的 \"没试过标准对策\" 攻击（预计 1-2 天 GPU，2 seeds，Walker 单环境）；(4) NVE 讨论加入 leave-one-environment-out\n7\t  cross-validation AUROC（已有 4 环境数据可离线计算）+ bootstrap 95% CI；(5) 论文标题考虑从 \"Diagnosing...\"\n8\t  改为 \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails...\" 以降低 novelty 期望值。Rebuttal 可将 borderline 翻转但需额外\n9\t  2-3 天实验。\n10\t\n11\t  '\n12\timagined_experiments:\n13\t- name: Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\n14\t  plan_id: plan_011\n15\t  description: 复制 008d 配置（subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8）到 seed 1 和 seed 2，验证\n16\t    CIVO 崩溃的跨 seed 可复现性\n17\t  expected_results:\n18\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 131\n19\t    seed1_nve_peak: 4.12\n20\t    seed1_nve_peak_step: 55K\n21\t    seed1_collapse: true\n22\t    seed1_collapse_onset: 25K\n23\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 268\n24\t    seed2_nve_peak: 2.05\n25\t    seed2_nve_peak_step: 25K\n26\t    seed2_collapse: false\n27\t    seed2_self_correction: true\n28\t    seed2_nve_105K: 0.38\n29\t    collapse_rate: 1/2 (50%)\n30\t    nve_gt_1.5x_rate: 2/2 (100%)\n31\t    nve_threshold_separation: 4/4 perfect (trained 2/2 > 1.5x, untrained 0/2 < 1.5x)\n32\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档认可 nve>1.5x 阈值的 4/4 分离力作为诊断工具，但对崩溃率 50%（仅 2 个独立 seed）的统计\n33\t    power 提出质疑。 Seed 1 重现经典 CIVO（value 爆炸 → eval 下降），seed 2 自我修正（transient nve>1.5x\n34\t    → 回落）。 审稿人会指出：2 seeds 只能给出 50% 的点估计，95% CI 覆盖 [7%, 93%]（Clopper-Pearson），无法区分\n35\t    \"rare event\" 和 \"coin flip\"。 这是 median 档 major weakness #1：per-method 样本量不足。Full\n36\t    SGS 仅 3 seeds、RAVE 仅 2 configs 同样被标记。\n37\t\n38\t    '\n39\t  tables:\n40\t  - name: 008d cross-seed NVE trajectory\n41\t    columns:\n42\t    - Step\n43\t    - Seed 0 NVE\n44\t    - Seed 1 NVE\n45\t    - Seed 2 NVE\n46\t    rows:\n47\t    - - 25K\n48\t      - '1.78'\n49\t      - '1.78'\n50\t      - '2.05'\n51\t    - - 35K\n52\t      - '1.71'\n53\t      - '1.71'\n54\t      - '1.24'\n55\t    - - 45K\n56\t      - '2.09'\n57\t      - '2.09'\n58\t      - '1.62'\n59\t    - - 55K\n60\t      - '4.12'\n61\t      - '4.12'\n62\t      - '1.41'\n63\t    - - 65K\n64\t      - '-'\n65\t      - '1.23'\n66\t      - '0.94'\n67\t    - - 85K\n68\t      - '-'\n69\t      - '1.15'\n70\t      - '0.51'\n71\t    - - 105K\n72\t      - '-'\n73\t      - '1.57'\n74\t      - '0.38'\n75\t  figures_description:\n76\t  - NVE 时间序列图：3 seeds 并排，标注 1.5x 阈值线。Seed 0/1 持续超阈值，seed 2 transient 后回落。\n77\t  analysis: 'CIVO 诊断标记（nve>1.5x）具有 100% 敏感性（2/2 trained seeds 均触发），但崩溃本身是随机的。 Median\n78\t    档审稿人接受因果方向（trained dt_emb → pathological overestimation）但质疑： (a) 仅 2 seeds 的崩溃率不具统计意义；(b)\n79\t    self-correction 机制未解释——如果 CIVO 可以 self-correct， 为什么还需要干预？需要在 rebuttal 中强调：self-correction\n80\t    不可靠（seed 2 eval 仅恢复到 268 = 29% baseline）， 且 sustained vs transient overestimation\n81\t    的分界点无法事先预测。\n82\t\n83\t    '\n84\t- name: Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\n85\t  plan_id: plan_012\n86\t  description: 复制 008f 因果控制（subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8）到 seed 1-2，验证无 dt_embedding\n87\t    时的稳定性\n88\t  expected_results:\n89\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 503\n90\t    seed1_nve_105K: 0.3\n91\t    seed1_collapse: false\n92\t    seed1_trend: zigzag recovery 173→375→324→246→319→503\n93\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 148\n94\t    seed2_nve_105K: 1.14\n95\t    seed2_collapse: false\n96\t    seed2_trend: peak 359@75K then monotonic decline to 148\n97\t    reward_MAE: 0.747\n98\t    reward_MAE_vs_baseline: 75x\n99\t    cross_seed_consistency: poor — seed 1 recovers to 503, seed 2 declines to 148\n100\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档的关键攻击点在 008f 的 reward_MAE（baseline 的 75x）和跨 seed 不一致性。\n101\t    Seed 1 的 zigzag recovery 到 503（55% baseline）是合理的；seed 2 declining 到 148（16% baseline）\n102\t    则暴露 008f 不是一个可靠的 \"保护\" 方案。审稿人会问：\"如果去掉 dt_embedding 导致 reward prediction 崩塌（MAE=0.747），\n103\t    那么 008f 的''稳定性''是否只是因为 critic 已经无法学到有意义的值——是''保护''还是''功能丧失''？\" 这个质疑在 median 档是合理的——008f\n104\t    的定位必须严格限制在\"因果控制实验\"（证明 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件）， 不能作为推荐方案。Seed 2 的 nve=1.14x@105K（borderline）也会被拿来质疑阈值的鲁棒性。\n105\t\n106\t    '\n107\t  tables:\n108\t  - name: 008f cross-seed comparison\n109\t    columns:\n110\t    - Metric\n111\t    - Seed 0 (s0)\n112\t    - Seed 1\n113\t    - Seed 2\n114\t    rows:\n115\t    - - eval@105K\n116\t      - '503'\n117\t      - 503*\n118\t      - '148'\n119\t    - - NVE@105K\n120\t      - '0.30'\n121\t      - 0.30*\n122\t      - '1.14'\n123\t    - - Peak eval\n124\t      - 503@105K\n125\t      - 503@105K*\n126\t      - 359@75K\n127\t    - - Trend\n128\t      - zigzag recovery\n129\t      - zigzag recovery*\n130\t      - monotonic decline\n131\t    note: '*seed 0 和 seed 1 实为同一 seed（deterministic reproduction），仅 seed 2 为独立 seed'\n132\t  figures_description:\n133\t  - 008f seed 1 vs seed 2 eval 曲线对比，标注 reward_MAE=0.747 作为功能退化警告\n134\t  analysis: '008f 作为因果控制实验成功证明了 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件（两个 seed 均未出现 nve>1.5x），\n135\t    但跨 seed 性能差异巨大（503 vs 148），且 reward prediction 严重退化。 Median 档审稿人至少会标记这一点为 major\n136\t    weakness：causal control 的清洁度被 reward 退化污染。 Rebuttal 策略：承认 008f 不是方案而是诊断工具，将推荐方案指向\n137\t    008e_v3（C6）或完全移除 dt_embedding（C7 after D107）。\n138\t\n139\t    '\n140\t- name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\n141\t  plan_id: plan_014\n142\t  description: 验证 008e_v3（trained dt_emb + dt=1 imagination + subsample ON + H=15）在\n143\t    seed 1-2 的 mitigation 效果\n144\t  expected_results:\n145\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 870\n146\t    seed1_nve_105K: 0.8\n147\t    seed1_collapse: false\n148\t    seed1_vs_baseline: 95%\n149\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 137\n150\t    seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n151\t    seed2_collapse: true\n152\t    seed2_collapse_onset: 95K\n153\t    seed2_mechanism: non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy ↑, policy destabilization)\n154\t    collapse_rate: 1/2 (50%)\n155\t    mitigation_verdict: PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\n156\t  result_rationale: '这是 median 档最关键的结果之一。dt=1 imagination 曾被假设为实用 mitigation（seed\n157\t    1: 95% baseline, nve=0.80x）， 但 seed 2 崩溃否证了该假设。审稿人会抓住两点： (1) 50% 崩溃率与 008d（dt=2\n158\t    imagination）的 50% 崩溃率相同——dt=1 imagination 未降低崩溃概率； (2) seed 2 的崩溃机制（entropy 上升、eval\n159\t    先跌、value 温和变化）与经典 CIVO 定性不同， 说明 trained dt_embedding 通过多条路径创造脆弱性。 Median 档审稿人认为这是\n160\t    \"interesting observation\"（多路径脆弱性），但不够强——仅 2 seeds， 且两种崩溃机制的区分缺乏正式统计检验。\n161\t\n162\t    '\n163\t  tables:\n164\t  - name: 008e_v3 collapse dynamics comparison\n165\t    columns:\n166\t    - Feature\n167\t    - Seed 1 (healthy)\n168\t    - Seed 2 (collapsed)\n169\t    - 008d s0 (classic CIVO)\n170\t    rows:\n171\t    - - eval@105K\n172\t      - 870 (95% baseline)\n173\t      - 137 (15% baseline)\n174\t      - 83 (9% baseline)\n175\t    - - NVE@105K\n176\t      - '0.80'\n177\t      - '3.78'\n178\t      - '4.12'\n179\t    - - Value trajectory\n180\t      - monotonically rising\n181\t      - 339→384→340 (±13%)\n182\t      - 25→60→98→138 (+130%)\n183\t    - - Entropy@collapse\n184\t      - -5.2 (stable)\n185\t      - -5.2→-3.8 (rising)\n186\t      - -3.5→-4.9 (falling)\n187\t    - - Collapse driver\n188\t      - N/A\n189\t      - eval crash → NVE spike\n190\t      - value explosion → eval drop\n191\t    - - Pathway\n192\t      - —\n193\t      - B (IRD, policy instability)\n194\t      - A (CIVO, value-driven)\n195\t  figures_description:\n196\t  - '3 panel figure: seed 1 healthy trajectory, seed 2 collapse with entropy annotation,\n197\t    008d classic CIVO for contrast'\n198\t  analysis: 'C6 partially falsified 是论文的重要转折点——从 \"practical mitigation\" 转为 \"diagnostic\n199\t    evidence\"。 Median 档的 narrative 建议是将此发现框架为 \"trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability\n200\t    through multiple pathways\"， 但审稿人会认为 2 seeds 不足以可靠区分两种 pathway。 额外 seeds (plan_016)\n201\t    的 2/4 崩溃率确认了 50% 但仍不足以做正式统计——median 档要求至少 6-8 seeds per config。\n202\t\n203\t    '\n204\t- name: Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\n205\t  plan_id: plan_013\n206\t  description: 验证 008a（subsample OFF + unexposed trained dt_emb + H=15）的值抑制和 V-recovery\n207\t    模式\n208\t  expected_results:\n209\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 631\n210\t    seed1_nve_105K: 0.43\n211\t    seed1_civo_alert: 0\n212\t    seed1_trend: gradual rise 140→394→414→441→492→453→547→629→631\n213\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 899\n214\t    seed2_nve_105K: 0.33\n215\t    seed2_civo_alert: 0\n216\t    seed2_trend: faster convergence 311→432→608→654→534→605→819→899\n217\t    cross_seed_mean_105K: 770\n218\t    cross_seed_std: 137\n219\t    vs_baseline_mean: 84%\n220\t    nve_range_all_seeds: 0.33-0.93\n221\t  result_rationale: 'Unexposed trained dt_emb（subsample OFF 意味着 dt_emb 从未见过 dt>1 数据）应表现类似\n222\t    untrained dt_emb： NVE 抑制 + 无 CIVO。Seed 0 (778@105K)、seed 1 (631)、seed 2 (899)\n223\t    均无崩溃，NVE 全程 < 1.0x。 但跨 seed 方差大（631-899, CV≈18%），median 档审稿人会指出：(a) 3 seeds 的均值\n224\t    770±137 只能说 \"大致恢复\"， precision 不够；(b) 008a 的 zigzag pattern 是 DreamerV3 的一般特征还是特定于此配置？\n225\t    缺乏 baseline 同 seed 对照的 zigzag 频率对比。这不会是 major weakness 但会被标注。\n226\t\n227\t    '\n228\t  tables:\n229\t  - name: 008a cross-seed summary\n230\t    columns:\n231\t    - Metric\n232\t    - Seed 0\n233\t    - Seed 1\n234\t    - Seed 2\n235\t    - Mean ± Std\n236\t    rows:\n237\t    - - eval@105K\n238\t      - '778'\n239\t      - '631'\n240\t      - '899'\n241\t      - 770 ± 137\n242\t    - - NVE@105K\n243\t      - '0.59'\n244\t      - '0.43'\n245\t      - '0.33'\n246\t      - 0.45 ± 0.13\n247\t    - - Peak eval\n248\t      - 778@105K\n249\t      - 631@105K\n250\t      - 899@105K\n251\t      - —\n252\t    - - vs baseline\n253\t      - 85%\n254\t      - 69%\n255\t      - 98%\n256\t      - 84% ± 15%\n257\t    - - CIVO alert\n258\t      - '0'\n259\t      - '0'\n260\t      - '0'\n261\t      - 0/3\n262\t  figures_description:\n263\t  - 008a 3-seed eval learning curves with IQM band, overlaid with baseline for reference\n264\t  analysis: 'C3（untrained/unexposed dt_emb 保护）在 3 seeds 中全部确认：NVE 持续 <1.0x，无 CIVO。\n265\t    Median 档接受 C3 的因果方向但认为 84% baseline recovery 不够有说服力—— \"如果最优 mitigation 还是损失 16%\n266\t    performance，这更像是 ''less bad'' 而不是 ''solution''\"。 审稿人建议与完全移除 dt_emb 的 008f 对比成本效益。\n267\t\n268\t    '\n269\t- name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\n270\t  plan_id: plan_016\n271\t  description: 扩展 008e_v3 到 seed 3-4，缩窄崩溃概率估计的置信区间\n272\t  expected_results:\n273\t    seed3_eval_return_105K: 93\n274\t    seed3_nve_peak: 4.02\n275\t    seed3_collapse: true\n276\t    seed3_collapse_onset: 85K-95K\n277\t    seed3_entropy_signature: -4.89 (falling — closer to Pathway A/CIVO)\n278\t    seed4_eval_return_105K: 899\n279\t    seed4_nve_peak: 0.99\n280\t    seed4_collapse: false\n281\t    collapse_rate_4seeds: 2/4 (50%)\n282\t    collapse_95CI: '[7%, 93%] (Clopper-Pearson exact)'\n283\t  result_rationale: '4 seeds 中 2 个崩溃（s2 和 s3）、2 个存活（s1 和 s4），确认 50% 崩溃率的点估计。 但 Clopper-Pearson\n284\t    95% CI 仍为 [7%, 93%]，审稿人正确指出这个区间太宽，无法做有意义的推断。 Seed 3 的崩溃（entropy 下降）看起来更接近 Pathway\n285\t    A（CIVO），而 seed 2（entropy 上升）是 Pathway B（IRD）， 但 n=2 per pathway 完全不够做统计区分。 Median\n286\t    档的核心批评：50% 崩溃率意味着 dt=1 imagination 和 dt=2 imagination 的脆弱性相同， 那么 \"架构边界\" 叙事的增量价值在哪里？\n287\t\n288\t    '\n289\t  tables:\n290\t  - name: 008e_v3 all-seed collapse summary\n291\t    columns:\n292\t    - Seed\n293\t    - eval@105K\n294\t    - NVE peak\n295\t    - Collapse?\n296\t    - Pathway\n297\t    rows:\n298\t    - - s1\n299\t      - '870'\n300\t      - '0.80'\n301\t      - 'No'\n302\t      - —\n303\t    - - s2\n304\t      - '137'\n305\t      - '3.78'\n306\t      - 'Yes'\n307\t      - B (IRD, entropy ↑)\n308\t    - - s3\n309\t      - '93'\n310\t      - '4.02'\n311\t      - 'Yes'\n312\t      - A-like (entropy ↓)\n313\t    - - s4\n314\t      - '899'\n315\t      - '0.99'\n316\t      - 'No'\n317\t      - —\n318\t    - - Rate\n319\t      - —\n320\t      - —\n321\t      - 2/4 = 50%\n322\t      - Mixed\n323\t  figures_description:\n324\t  - 4-seed eval trajectory panel with collapse onset markers, color-coded by pathway\n325\t    type\n326\t  analysis: 'Plan_016 的 4 seeds 收窄了估计但统计力仍不足。Median 档审稿人会标记： \"4 seeds per config ×\n327\t    50% collapse rate = 单位实验成本下统计效率极低， 需要 ≥12 seeds 才能将 CI 缩窄到有意义区间 [30%, 70%]。\" 对\n328\t    rebuttal 价值有限——确认了 50% 但无法 defend against \"statistically underpowered\"。\n329\t\n330\t    '\n331\t- name: Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\n332\t  plan_id: plan_015\n333\t  description: freeze dt_embedding（requires_grad=False），保持随机初始化。诊断 dt_emb 的 TRAINING\n334\t    是否是 CIVO 的必要条件\n335\t  expected_results:\n336\t    eval_return_105K: 204\n337\t    nve_105K: 0.42\n338\t    nve_range: 0.39-0.47\n339\t    collapse: false\n340\t    actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n341\t    actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n342\t    value_mean_105K: 56.2\n343\t    gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n344\t    failure_mode: gradient_starvation — actor_loss→0, critic underestimates\n345\t    vs_baseline: 22%\n346\t  result_rationale: 'Frozen dt_emb 阻止了 CIVO（NVE 0.39-0.47，远低于 1.5x），确认了 dt_emb TRAINING\n347\t    是 CIVO 的必要条件。 但引入了新失败模式：gradient starvation。随机初始化的 frozen embedding 给 RSSM 提供无信息量的\n348\t    conditioning signal， actor_loss→0 意味着 actor 梯度消失，策略无法有效改进。 Median 档审稿人会认为这是 \"expected\n349\t    but useful\"——frozen random embedding 当然不好用， 但它闭合了 2×2 消融矩阵（trained/frozen × exposed/unexposed）。\n350\t    Novelty 评价：2.5-3.0。这个结果是消融设计的自然推论，不是独立贡献。\n351\t\n352\t    '\n353\t  tables:\n354\t  - name: dt_emb training ablation matrix\n355\t    columns:\n356\t    - ''\n357\t    - Exposed to dt>1 (subsample ON)\n358\t    - Unexposed (subsample OFF)\n359\t    rows:\n360\t    - - Trained dt_emb\n361\t      - '008d: CIVO collapse (NVE 2.09x)'\n362\t      - '008a: V-recovery (NVE 0.59x)'\n363\t    - - Frozen dt_emb\n364\t      - '015b: gradient starvation (NVE 0.42x)'\n365\t      - (= 008a equivalent, cancelled)\n366\t    - - No dt_emb (dim=0)\n367\t      - '008f: reward degradation (NVE 0.30x)'\n368\t      - N/A\n369\t  figures_description:\n370\t  - 2×2 消融矩阵热力图：NVE peak × eval@105K，标注每个 cell 的失败模式\n371\t  analysis: '015b 闭合了关键消融，但 median 档审稿人会指出矩阵的解读过度简化： 仅 1 seed per cell（除 008d 有多 seed），且不同\n372\t    cell 的失败模式（CIVO vs gradient starvation vs reward degradation） 不可比——不能简单用 NVE 一个指标统一评估。\n373\t\n374\t    '\n375\t- name: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n376\t  plan_id: plan_020\n377\t  description: Cheetah Run dt=1 baseline，建立第二环境的 v/e calibration\n378\t  expected_results:\n379\t    seed0_eval_return_200K: 625\n380\t    seed1_eval_return_200K: 520\n381\t    seed2_eval_return_200K: 645\n382\t    cross_seed_mean: 597\n383\t    cross_seed_std: 68\n384\t    ve_ratio_converged: 0.60-0.70\n385\t    convergence_step: 150K-200K\n386\t  result_rationale: 'Cheetah Run baseline 表现低于 Walker Walk（~600 vs ~950），variance\n387\t    更高。 已有 5 seeds 数据（s0=625, s1=520, s2=645, s3=642, s4=537），均值 594±54。 Median 档审稿人接受\n388\t    baseline 稳定性但会注意到 s4 的 194K→204K 骤降（537→302 transient drop）， 质疑 Cheetah 基线本身的不稳定性是否混淆了\n389\t    CIVO 诊断。 Converged v/e 约 0.60-0.70，为 NVE normalization 提供基准。\n390\t\n391\t    '\n392\t  tables:\n393\t  - name: Cheetah baseline cross-seed\n394\t    columns:\n395\t    - Seed\n396\t    - eval_final\n397\t    - eval_peak\n398\t    - ve_ratio_converged\n399\t    rows:\n400\t    - - s0\n401\t      - '625'\n402\t      - '625'\n403\t      - ~0.65\n404\t    - - s1\n405\t      - '520'\n406\t      - '573'\n407\t      - ~0.60\n408\t    - - s2\n409\t      - '645'\n410\t      - '645'\n411\t      - ~0.65\n412\t    - - Mean\n413\t      - '597'\n414\t      - '614'\n415\t      - ~0.63\n416\t  figures_description:\n417\t  - Cheetah baseline 3-seed learning curves with IQM confidence band\n418\t  analysis: 'Baseline 确立但 inter-seed variance（CV≈11%）高于 Walker（CV≈3%）， 这意味着 Cheetah\n419\t    的 CIVO 检测需要更多 seeds 才能达到 Walker 的统计 power。 Median 档审稿人会指出此 asymmetry。\n420\t\n421\t    '\n422\t- name: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n423\t  plan_id: plan_021\n424\t  description: Cheetah Run 中复制 CIVO trigger（dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb）\n425\t  expected_results:\n426\t    seed0_eval_return_105K: 1\n427\t    seed0_nve_peak: 70.64\n428\t    seed0_civo: true\n429\t    seed0_collapse_type: catastrophic\n430\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 52\n431\t    seed1_nve_peak: 8.27\n432\t    seed1_civo: true\n433\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 85\n434\t    seed2_nve_peak: 12.5\n435\t    seed2_civo: true\n436\t    civo_rate: 3/3 (100%)\n437\t    mean_nve_peak: 30.5\n438\t    cheetah_vs_walker_severity: Cheetah CIVO severity >> Walker (mean NVE 30x vs 3x)\n439\t  result_rationale: 'Cheetah 已有 2 seeds 数据（s0: NVE=70.64 catastrophic, s1/exp_010b:\n440\t    NVE=8.27 severe）。 Cheetah 的 CIVO 比 Walker 严重得多——NVE 峰值 8-70x vs Walker 的 2-4x。\n441\t    这是因为 Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 更大（更高维运动学 → dt>1 预测更难）。 预测 seed 2 也会 CIVO（NVE\n442\t    ~10-15x），给出 3/3 = 100% 崩溃率。 Median 档认为这强化了 C1/C2 的跨环境泛化，但会质疑： (a) Cheetah 的 CIVO\n443\t    动力学与 Walker 定性不同（更早、更严重），是否真是同一机制？ (b) 仅 2 个环境（Walker + Cheetah）不够 claim \"generalizes\"——3\n444\t    环境是最低限度。\n445\t\n446\t    '\n447\t  tables:\n448\t  - name: Cheetah CIVO trigger cross-seed\n449\t    columns:\n450\t    - Seed\n451\t    - eval@105K\n452\t    - NVE peak\n453\t    - Collapse type\n454\t    rows:\n455\t    - - s0\n456\t      - ~1\n457\t      - '70.64'\n458\t      - catastrophic\n459\t    - - s1\n460\t      - '52'\n461\t      - '8.27'\n462\t      - severe\n463\t    - - s2 (predicted)\n464\t      - ~85\n465\t      - ~12.5\n466\t      - severe\n467\t  figures_description:\n468\t  - Cheetah NVE time series 3 seeds vs Walker 3 seeds, showing environment-dependent\n469\t    severity\n470\t  analysis: 'Cheetah 的 100% 崩溃率（vs Walker 50%）和更高 NVE 峰值是双刃剑： 强化了 CIVO 是真实威胁，但也暗示\n471\t    Walker 的 50% 可能是偏低的 — 环境越难 CIVO 越强。 Median 档审稿人接受跨环境 CIVO 存在性但认为 severity 差异（10x）需要解释：\n472\t    是 RSSM capacity 差异还是 task complexity 差异？\n473\t\n474\t    '\n475\t- name: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n476\t  plan_id: plan_022\n477\t  description: Cheetah Run 因果控制：去掉 dt_embedding 是否阻止 CIVO\n478\t  expected_results:\n479\t    seed0_eval_return_105K: 97\n480\t    seed0_nve_peak: 0.2\n481\t    seed0_civo: false\n482\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 77\n483\t    seed1_nve_peak: 0.1\n484\t    seed1_civo: false\n485\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 90\n486\t    seed2_nve_peak: 0.15\n487\t    seed2_civo: false\n488\t    civo_prevention_rate: 3/3 (100%)\n489\t    mean_eval_vs_baseline: 15%\n490\t    reward_MAE_vs_baseline: '>50x'\n491\t  result_rationale: '已有 2 seeds：s0 eval=96.5（NVE 0.2, no CIVO），s1 eval=77.3（NVE 0.1,\n492\t    no CIVO）。 与 Walker 008f 一致：去掉 dt_embedding 完全阻止 CIVO，但 eval 严重退化（仅 ~15% baseline）。\n493\t    Cheetah 的退化比 Walker 更严重（Walker 008f 达 55% baseline），因为 Cheetah 对 reward prediction\n494\t    更敏感。 Median 档接受因果控制成立（5/5 across 2 environments: no dt_emb → no CIVO）， 但再次质疑：这是\n495\t    \"prevention\" 还是 \"feature removal leading to functional impairment\"？\n496\t\n497\t    '\n498\t  tables:\n499\t  - name: Cross-environment causal control (dt_embed_dim=0)\n500\t    columns:\n501\t    - Environment\n502\t    - Seeds\n503\t    - CIVO rate\n504\t    - Mean eval vs baseline\n505\t    - Reward MAE ratio\n506\t    rows:\n507\t    - - Walker Walk\n508\t      - 3 (s0, s3, s4)\n509\t      - 0/3\n510\t      - ~40%\n511\t      - 75x\n512\t    - - Cheetah Run\n513\t      - 2-3\n514\t      - 0/3\n515\t      - ~15%\n516\t      - '>50x'\n517\t    - - Combined\n518\t      - 5-6\n519\t      - 0/5+\n520\t      - ~30%\n521\t      - '>>1x'\n522\t  figures_description:\n523\t  - 'Bar chart: CIVO rate and eval retention for dt_embed_dim=0 across environments'\n524\t  analysis: '因果控制在 Cheetah 中复现，5/5 完美分离确认 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件。 但 eval 退化在 Cheetah\n525\t    更严重，暴露了一个 tension：去掉 dt_embedding \"治愈\" CIVO 但也移除了 dt-conditioning 的功能价值。这对 \"CIVO\n526\t    是 dt-conditioning 不可避免的副作用\" 的叙事有利， 但审稿人会要求解释为什么不能 have both（有效 conditioning +\n527\t    无 CIVO）。\n528\t\n529\t    '\n530\t- name: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\n531\t  plan_id: plan_023\n532\t  description: Cheetah Run 中验证 unexposed trained dt_emb 的值抑制效果\n533\t  expected_results:\n534\t    seed0_eval_return_105K: 532\n535\t    seed0_nve_105K: 0.49\n536\t    seed0_civo: false\n537\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 504\n538\t    seed1_nve_105K: 0.48\n539\t    seed1_civo: false\n540\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 480\n541\t    seed2_nve_105K: 0.52\n542\t    seed2_civo: false\n543\t    mean_eval_vs_baseline: 85%\n544\t    nve_range: 0.48-0.52\n545\t  result_rationale: '已有 2 seeds：s0=532（NVE 0.49），s1=504（NVE 0.48）。Unexposed dt_emb\n546\t    在 Cheetah 中也有效： NVE < 1.0x，eval 保留 ~85% baseline。与 Walker 008a 一致（84% baseline）。\n547\t    这是 C3 跨环境验证的最强数据：两个环境的 unexposed dt_emb 均表现出值抑制 + 高 eval 保留。 Median 档接受 C3 但认为\n548\t    \"unexposed = subsample OFF\" 只是一种 workaround， 不是对 CIVO 机制的根本解决。\"如果你不让模型见到 dt>1\n549\t    数据，当然不会 CIVO——但这也失去了 temporal abstraction 的目的。\"\n550\t\n551\t    '\n552\t  tables:\n553\t  - name: 'C3 cross-environment: unexposed dt_emb'\n554\t    columns:\n555\t    - Environment\n556\t    - Seeds\n557\t    - Mean eval vs baseline\n558\t    - NVE range\n559\t    - CIVO\n560\t    rows:\n561\t    - - Walker Walk\n562\t      - '3'\n563\t      - 84%\n564\t      - 0.33-0.93\n565\t      - 0/3\n566\t    - - Cheetah Run\n567\t      - 2-3\n568\t      - 85%\n569\t      - 0.48-0.52\n570\t      - 0/3\n571\t  figures_description:\n572\t  - 'Cross-environment eval retention bar chart: unexposed dt_emb vs baseline vs trained\n573\t    dt_emb'\n574\t  analysis: 'C3 获得跨环境确认（6 seeds, 0 CIVO, 84-85% baseline），是论文中最 robust 的正面结果。 但 median\n575\t    档正确指出这不是 mitigation——它避开了问题而非解决问题。\n576\t\n577\t    '\n578\t- name: 'RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions'\n579\t  plan_id: plan_030\n580\t  description: 量化不同模型在 dt=1 和 dt=2 上的 RSSM 预测质量差距\n581\t  expected_results:\n582\t    baseline_obs_gap: 2.04\n583\t    baseline_reward_gap: 1.56\n584\t    008d_obs_gap: 1.3\n585\t    008d_reward_gap: 2.78\n586\t    008f_obs_gap: 2.75\n587\t    008f_reward_gap: 1.01\n588\t    008d_dt1_obs_MSE: 41.31\n589\t    baseline_dt1_obs_MSE: 13.49\n590\t    key_finding: 008d 的低 obs gap (1.30x) 具误导性——其 dt=1 绝对误差已是 baseline 3x\n591\t  result_rationale: 'RSSM fidelity 分析已完成（exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis）。核心发现： 008d 的\n592\t    obs gap ratio 看起来最小（1.30x），但绝对误差最大（dt1: 41.31 vs baseline 13.49）， 说明模型整体已崩塌，gap\n593\t    ratio 失去意义。008f 的 reward gap (1.01x) 说明无 dt_embedding 时 reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2——这是\n594\t    \"功能丧失\" 不是 \"改善\"。 Median 档审稿人认为这是 \"expected and confirmatory\"——RSSM 在 dt>1 预测不好是已知的，\n595\t    novelty 不在发现本身而在它与 CIVO 的因果连接。但审稿人会质疑： 只有 1 个 checkpoint 的分析，如何确认这是训练全程的 pattern\n596\t    而非特定 step 的 artifact？\n597\t\n598\t    '\n599\t  tables:\n600\t  - name: RSSM Fidelity Table\n601\t    columns:\n602\t    - Model\n603\t    - dt1 obs_MSE\n604\t    - dt2 obs_MSE\n605\t    - obs gap\n606\t    - dt1 reward_MAE\n607\t    - dt2 reward_MAE\n608\t    - reward gap\n609\t    rows:\n610\t    - - baseline\n611\t      - '13.49'\n612\t      - '27.50'\n613\t      - 2.04x\n614\t      - '0.0102'\n615\t      - '0.0159'\n616\t      - 1.56x\n617\t    - - 008d (trained dt_emb)\n618\t      - '41.31'\n619\t      - '53.67'\n620\t      - 1.30x\n621\t      - '0.0568'\n622\t      - '0.1579'\n623\t      - 2.78x\n624\t    - - 008f (no dt_emb)\n625\t      - '8.01'\n626\t      - '22.04'\n627\t      - 2.75x\n628\t      - '0.7469'\n629\t      - '0.7526'\n630\t      - 1.01x\n631\t  figures_description:\n632\t  - Bar chart with both absolute values and ratios side-by-side, preventing ratio-only\n633\t    misleading\n634\t  analysis: 'RSSM fidelity 分析确认了机制假说但未超越 \"supporting evidence\"。 Median 档给这个分析 moderate\n635\t    credit 但不视为独立贡献。 建议在 rebuttal 中加入训练过程中 fidelity 的演化曲线（多 checkpoint），回应 \"single\n636\t    snapshot\" 质疑。\n637\t\n638\t    '\n639\t- name: Actor entropy analysis\n640\t  plan_id: plan_031\n641\t  description: 对比健康 vs 崩溃配置的 actor entropy 演化\n642\t  expected_results:\n643\t    healthy_008a_entropy_trend: 稳定在 -4.5 to -5.2 范围\n644\t    healthy_008c_entropy_trend: 缓慢下降 -3.5 → -4.8\n645\t    collapsed_006_entropy_trend: 下降后回弹 -3.5 → -4.9 → -3.8\n646\t    collapsed_008d_entropy_trend: 持续下降 -1.9 → -4.9\n647\t    collapsed_008e_v3_s2_entropy_trend: 先降后升 -5.2 → -3.8 (反常)\n648\t    pathway_A_signature: entropy ↓ (policy 过度确定化)\n649\t    pathway_B_signature: entropy ↑ (policy destabilization)\n650\t  result_rationale: 'Actor entropy 分析是区分 Pathway A (CIVO) 和 Pathway B (IRD) 的关键诊断工具。\n651\t    经典 CIVO (008d): value overestimate → actor exploit → entropy 下降 → 策略变得过度确定。 非\n652\t    CIVO 崩溃 (008e_v3_s2): eval 先跌 → value 滞后 → entropy 上升 → 策略变得随机。 Median 档认为这是 \"useful\n653\t    characterization\" 但不是 \"novel contribution\"—— entropy 作为策略健康度指标是标准做法，两种 pathway\n654\t    的区分缺乏 formal framework。\n655\t\n656\t    '\n657\t  tables:\n658\t  - name: Entropy trajectory comparison\n659\t    columns:\n660\t    - Config\n661\t    - Entropy@35K\n662\t    - Entropy@55K\n663\t    - Entropy@85K\n664\t    - Entropy@105K\n665\t    - Pathway\n666\t    rows:\n667\t    - - 008a s0 (healthy)\n668\t      - '-4.2'\n669\t      - '-4.5'\n670\t      - '-4.8'\n671\t      - '-5.0'\n672\t      - —\n673\t    - - 008d s0 (CIVO)\n674\t      - '-3.5'\n675\t      - '-4.9'\n676\t      - —\n677\t      - —\n678\t      - A\n679\t    - - 008e_v3 s2 (IRD)\n680\t      - '-3.5'\n681\t      - '-5.1'\n682\t      - '-5.2'\n683\t      - '-3.8'\n684\t      - B\n685\t    - - 016e (SGS)\n686\t      - '-2.1'\n687\t      - '-3.6'\n688\t      - '-4.3'\n689\t      - —\n690\t      - A (delayed)\n691\t  figures_description:\n692\t  - 'Entropy vs step: healthy configs (blue band) vs CIVO (red, entropy ↓) vs IRD\n693\t    (orange, entropy ↑)'\n694\t  analysis: 'Entropy 分析确认两种崩溃 pathway 的存在，但 n=1-2 per pathway 不足以 formalize。 Median\n695\t    档审稿人建议：如果要将 dual-pathway 作为贡献，需要至少 5 seeds per pathway 并做 statistical test。\n696\t\n697\t    '\n698\t- name: Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\n699\t  plan_id: plan_032\n700\t  description: V(s) vs Monte Carlo return 分布对比\n701\t  expected_results:\n702\t    trained_dt_emb_divergence: V(s) 分布右偏移 + 重尾，MC return 集中在低区间\n703\t    untrained_dt_emb_match: V(s) 和 MC return 分布大致重叠，V(s) 略微左移\n704\t    collapsed_state: V(s) 均值远超 MC return p95，完全脱钩\n705\t    healthy_calibration: V(s) 中位数在 MC return IQR 内\n706\t  result_rationale: '这是对 v/e ratio proxy 的补充验证。直接展示 V(s) 分布 vs 实际回报分布比单一 ratio 更具信息量。\n707\t    Median 档审稿人在 R3 中质疑 v/e ratio 是 crude proxy——这个分析直接回应。 预期结果：trained dt_emb 的 V(s)\n708\t    明显偏高且扩散，untrained 的则接近校准。 但审稿人仍会指出：MC return 在 imagination 中不可直接计算（需要 ground truth\n709\t    environment）， 只能用 eval return 作为 proxy，引入额外近似误差。\n710\t\n711\t    '\n712\t  tables: []\n713\t  figures_description:\n714\t  - '2×2 violin plot panel: (trained/untrained) × (pre-collapse/post-collapse), V(s)\n715\t    distribution in orange vs MC return in blue'\n716\t  analysis: 'Distributional 分析增加了 R3 的防御深度，但实现依赖 eval return 作为 MC return proxy， 审稿人可能认为这只是换了一种方式展示同样的信息。Median\n717\t    档给 minor positive credit。\n718\t\n719\t    '\n720\t- name: dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\n721\t  plan_id: plan_033\n722\t  description: 分析 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 向量的演化\n723\t  expected_results:\n724\t    initial_cosine_sim: ~0.0 (random init)\n725\t    trained_25K_cosine_sim: ~0.3\n726\t    trained_55K_cosine_sim: ~0.65\n727\t    trained_105K_cosine_sim: ~0.75 (converging)\n728\t    l2_distance_trend: monotonically increasing\n729\t    frozen_cosine_sim: constant at ~0.0\n730\t  result_rationale: 'Trained dt_embedding 的 dt=1 和 dt=2 向量会在训练过程中逐渐分离（cosine sim 从\n731\t    ~0 增加， 但 L2 距离增加），说明 embedding 学到了 dt-specific representation。 Frozen embedding\n732\t    保持初始状态不变（cosine sim ≈ 0）。 Median 档认为这是 \"descriptive visualization\"——确认 embedding\n733\t    在训练，但不提供超越已知的 insight。 审稿人的反应：nice plot, but what does it tell us that we didn''t\n734\t    already know from the gradient analysis?\n735\t\n736\t    '\n737\t  tables: []\n738\t  figures_description:\n739\t  - 'Line plot: cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2 embedding vectors over training\n740\t    steps, for trained vs frozen'\n741\t  analysis: 'Low priority（P2）合理。Cosine similarity 分析提供视觉直觉但不支撑任何独立 claim。 Median 档中这会出现在\n742\t    appendix 如果提交，不会影响评分。\n743\t\n744\t    '\n745\t- name: NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\n746\t  plan_id: plan_034\n747\t  description: 在不同阈值（1.3x, 1.5x, 1.7x, 2.0x）下计算分类准确率和 AUROC\n748\t  expected_results:\n749\t    threshold_1.3x_accuracy: 0.86\n750\t    threshold_1.5x_accuracy: 0.93\n751\t    threshold_1.7x_accuracy: 0.9\n752\t    threshold_2.0x_accuracy: 0.83\n753\t    youden_optimal_threshold: 1.53\n754\t    AUROC_walker: 0.98\n755\t    AUROC_cheetah: 0.95\n756\t    AUROC_combined: 0.969\n757\t    AUROC_bootstrap_95CI: '[0.91, 1.00]'\n758\t    n_total_datapoints: 29\n759\t    leave_one_env_out_AUROC_walker_train: 0.97\n760\t    leave_one_env_out_AUROC_cheetah_test: 0.92\n761\t  result_rationale: 'NVE 阈值分析基于所有可用 seeds（~29 数据点跨 4 环境）。1.5x 是 near-optimal（Youden\n762\t    index 收敛到 1.53x）， AUROC 0.969 表明 NVE 是 strong discriminator。 但 median 档审稿人一致标记（Dream\n763\t    D8）：阈值在同数据集上 calibrate 和 validate = in-sample bias。 Leave-one-environment-out\n764\t    CV 部分回应这个问题（Cheetah 作为 held-out 时 AUROC 仍 ~0.92）， 但只有 2 个环境做 LOO-CV 统计意义有限。 Bootstrap\n765\t    95% CI [0.91, 1.00] 看起来 impressive 但样本量小时 bootstrap CI 本身偏乐观。 这是 median 档的核心方法论弱点之一。\n766\t\n767\t    '\n768\t  tables:\n769\t  - name: NVE threshold ROC analysis\n770\t    columns:\n771\t    - Threshold\n772\t    - Sensitivity\n773\t    - Specificity\n774\t    - Accuracy\n775\t    - Youden J\n776\t    rows:\n777\t    - - 1.3x\n778\t      - '0.94'\n779\t      - '0.80'\n780\t      - '0.86'\n781\t      - '0.74'\n782\t    - - 1.5x\n783\t      - '0.88'\n784\t      - '1.00'\n785\t      - '0.93'\n786\t      - '0.88'\n787\t    - - 1.53x (optimal)\n788\t      - '0.88'\n789\t      - '1.00'\n790\t      - '0.93'\n791\t      - '0.88'\n792\t    - - 1.7x\n793\t      - '0.81'\n794\t      - '1.00'\n795\t      - '0.90'\n796\t      - '0.81'\n797\t    - - 2.0x\n798\t      - '0.69'\n799\t      - '1.00'\n800\t      - '0.83'\n801\t      - '0.69'\n802\t  - name: Leave-one-environment-out AUROC\n803\t    columns:\n804\t    - Train env\n805\t    - Test env\n806\t    - AUROC\n807\t    rows:\n808\t    - - Walker\n809\t      - Cheetah\n810\t      - '0.92'\n811\t    - - Cheetah\n812\t      - Walker\n813\t      - '0.97'\n814\t    - - Combined\n815\t      - Combined (bootstrap)\n816\t      - 0.969 [0.91, 1.00]\n817\t  figures_description:\n818\t  - ROC curve with 95% bootstrap CI band, marking Youden-optimal threshold\n819\t  analysis: 'AUROC 0.969 是 C2 的最强定量结果，但 in-sample calibration 和 n=29 是不可回避的限制。 Median\n820\t    档审稿人接受 NVE 作为 diagnostic tool 但不接受 1.5x 作为 generalizable threshold。 Rebuttal 策略：承认\n821\t    limitation，强调 leave-one-env-out 结果（虽然 n 小但方向正确）， 将 NVE threshold generalization\n822\t    定位为 future work。\n823\t\n824\t    '\n825\t- name: Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\n826\t  plan_id: plan_050\n827\t  description: 第三个 DMC 环境的 dt=1 baseline，扩展到非 locomotion 任务\n828\t  expected_results:\n829\t    seed0_eval_return_500K: 860\n830\t    seed1_eval_return_500K: 845\n831\t    seed2_eval_return_500K: 870\n832\t    cross_seed_mean: 858\n833\t    cross_seed_std: 13\n834\t    ve_ratio_converged: 0.65-0.75\n835\t    convergence_step: 80K-120K\n836\t  result_rationale: 'Cartpole Swingup 是 DMC 中相对简单的任务，DreamerV3 baseline 应快速收敛到 ~850-870。\n837\t    Inter-seed variance 预计低于 Cheetah（simpler dynamics → more consistent learning）。\n838\t    v/e ratio 收敛到 0.65-0.75，与 Walker/Cheetah 一致。 Median 档审稿人认为加入第三个环境是正面的（从 \"minimum\n839\t    viable\" 的 3 环境升级）， 但 Cartpole 作为相对简单任务可能不够挑战性——\"如果 CIVO 在简单任务上弱或不出现， 这削弱了 generalization\n840\t    claim 而非加强。\"\n841\t\n842\t    '\n843\t  tables:\n844\t  - name: Cartpole baseline\n845\t    columns:\n846\t    - Seed\n847\t    - eval@500K\n848\t    - ve_ratio_converged\n849\t    - convergence_step\n850\t    rows:\n851\t    - - s0\n852\t      - '860'\n853\t      - '0.70'\n854\t      - 100K\n855\t    - - s1\n856\t      - '845'\n857\t      - '0.68'\n858\t      - 110K\n859\t    - - s2\n860\t      - '870'\n861\t      - '0.72'\n862\t      - 90K\n863\t  figures_description:\n864\t  - Cartpole baseline learning curves, 3 seeds with confidence band\n865\t  analysis: 'Baseline 稳定。关键问题是 CIVO 在 Cartpole 的表现——如果弱于 Walker/Cheetah， 会被解读为 \"CIVO\n866\t    severity is task-dependent\"（median 档认可的弱化叙事）。\n867\t\n868\t    '\n869\t- name: Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n870\t  plan_id: plan_051\n871\t  description: Cartpole Swingup 中复制 CIVO trigger\n872\t  expected_results:\n873\t    seed0_eval_return_105K: 520\n874\t    seed0_nve_peak: 2.8\n875\t    seed0_civo: true\n876\t    seed0_collapse_type: partial — degradation without catastrophic collapse\n877\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 680\n878\t    seed1_nve_peak: 1.8\n879\t    seed1_civo: true\n880\t    seed1_collapse_type: mild — NVE borderline, eval recovers\n881\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 350\n882\t    seed2_nve_peak: 4.1\n883\t    seed2_civo: true\n884\t    seed2_collapse_type: moderate — sustained degradation\n885\t    civo_rate: 3/3 (NVE > 1.5x)\n886\t    catastrophic_collapse_rate: 0/3 (no complete collapse to random policy)\n887\t    mean_eval_vs_baseline: 60%\n888\t  result_rationale: 'Cartpole 比 Cheetah 简单但比 Walker 的 observation space 更低维（5 vs 24\n889\t    dim）， RSSM 在 dt>1 的预测误差相对较小。预期 CIVO 出现（NVE > 1.5x）但严重程度低于 Walker/Cheetah： degradation\n890\t    而非 catastrophic collapse。这是因为 Cartpole 的值函数 landscape 更平滑， value overestimation\n891\t    更容易被 self-correction 机制缓解。 Median 档审稿人会抓住这一点：\"CIVO severity 与任务复杂度相关——在简单任务上是\n892\t    nuisance， 在复杂任务上才是 fatal。这限制了 diagnostic 的实际影响力。\" 但也会认可：CIVO 在所有 3 个环境中都出现（NVE\n893\t    > 1.5x），direction 一致。\n894\t\n895\t    '\n896\t  tables:\n897\t  - name: Cross-environment CIVO severity\n898\t    columns:\n899\t    - Environment\n900\t    - CIVO rate\n901\t    - Mean NVE peak\n902\t    - Catastrophic collapse rate\n903\t    - Mean eval retention\n904\t    rows:\n905\t    - - Walker Walk\n906\t      - 2/4 (50%)\n907\t      - '2.7'\n908\t      - 2/4\n909\t      - 47%\n910\t    - - Cheetah Run\n911\t      - 3/3 (100%)\n912\t      - '30.5'\n913\t      - 2/3\n914\t      - 5%\n915\t    - - Cartpole Swingup\n916\t      - 3/3 (100%)\n917\t      - '2.9'\n918\t      - 0/3\n919\t      - 60%\n920\t  figures_description:\n921\t  - 'Cross-environment CIVO heatmap: environment × seed, colored by NVE peak'\n922\t  analysis: 'Cartpole 确认 CIVO 的 universality 但暴露了 severity 的强环境依赖性。 Median 档审稿人将此解读为\n923\t    \"the phenomenon is real but its practical impact is task-dependent\"， 进一步将 novelty\n924\t    定位为 incremental observation 而非 general finding。 NVE 阈值 1.5x 在 Cartpole 中仍有效（3/3\n925\t    detection），增强了跨环境泛化的证据。\n926\t\n927\t    '\n928\t- name: Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n929\t  plan_id: plan_052\n930\t  description: Cartpole Swingup 因果控制（无 dt_embedding）\n931\t  expected_results:\n932\t    seed0_eval_return_105K: 650\n933\t    seed0_nve_peak: 0.35\n934\t    seed0_civo: false\n935\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 620\n936\t    seed1_nve_peak: 0.4\n937\t    seed1_civo: false\n938\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 660\n939\t    seed2_nve_peak: 0.3\n940\t    seed2_civo: false\n941\t    civo_prevention_rate: 3/3 (100%)\n942\t    mean_eval_vs_baseline: 75%\n943\t    reward_MAE_vs_baseline: ~30x\n944\t  result_rationale: '无 dt_embedding 应阻止 CIVO（与 Walker/Cheetah 一致）。Cartpole 的 eval\n945\t    保留（75%） 介于 Walker（40-55%）和 baseline 之间，因为 Cartpole 的 reward 结构更简单， reward prediction\n946\t    退化的影响相对较小。 Median 档审稿人：因果控制在第三个环境确认，累计 8/8 across 3 environments（no dt_emb → no\n947\t    CIVO）。 这是论文中最 robust 的因果结论之一。 但评论：\"因果控制只证明 dt_embedding 是 necessary condition，没有提供\n948\t    mitigation pathway。\"\n949\t\n950\t    '\n951\t  tables:\n952\t  - name: Cross-environment causal control summary (final)\n953\t    columns:\n954\t    - Environment\n955\t    - Seeds\n956\t    - CIVO prevented\n957\t    - Eval retention\n958\t    - Reward degradation\n959\t    rows:\n960\t    - - Walker Walk\n961\t      - '3'\n962\t      - 3/3\n963\t      - 40-55%\n964\t      - 75x MAE\n965\t    - - Cheetah Run\n966\t      - 2-3\n967\t      - 2-3/2-3\n968\t      - ~15%\n969\t      - '>50x MAE'\n970\t    - - Cartpole Swingup\n971\t      - '3'\n972\t      - 3/3\n973\t      - ~75%\n974\t      - ~30x MAE\n975\t    - - '**Total**'\n976\t      - '**8-9**'\n977\t      - '**8-9/8-9**'\n978\t      - '**varies**'\n979\t      - '**>>1x**'\n980\t  figures_description:\n981\t  - 'Stacked bar chart: eval retention by environment for dt_embed_dim=0'\n982\t  analysis: '8/8+ 因果控制是 C2 的最终定量支撑。但 eval retention 的环境依赖性（15%-75%） 意味着 \"removing\n983\t    dt_embedding\" 的代价不一致，进一步说明 CIVO 问题没有 one-size-fits-all solution。\n984\t\n985\t    '\n986\t- name: Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\n987\t  plan_id: plan_060\n988\t  description: 监控 imagination rollout 中的 RSSM 预测不确定性，超过阈值时截断\n989\t  expected_results:\n990\t    eval_return_105K: 380\n991\t    nve_peak: 1.8\n992\t    civo_delayed: true\n993\t    civo_prevented: false\n994\t    truncation_rate_avg: 40% of rollout steps truncated\n995\t    effective_horizon: H_eff ≈ 9 (from H=15)\n996\t    eval_vs_baseline: 41%\n997\t    eval_vs_008d: 2.7x better than 008d collapse\n998\t  result_rationale: 'Uncertainty-gated truncation 在概念上是对的（截断不确定预测避免 error compounding），\n999\t    但在 DreamerV3 的 RSSM 中面临两个问题： (1) RSSM 的 posterior entropy 不是 calibrated 的 uncertainty\n1000\t    estimate—— 高 entropy 可能反映 genuine uncertainty 也可能反映 poor representation； (2) 截断降低了\n1001\t    effective horizon，相当于变相回到 H=8 的配置（已知性能较差）。 预测结果：CIVO 延迟但不完全阻止（NVE 仍达 1.8x），eval\n1002\t    中等（380 ≈ 41% baseline）。 Median 档审稿人：interesting pilot 但 1 seed 不足以 draw conclusions。\n1003\t    This could strengthen the intervention hierarchy as a 4th level (model-level gating)\n1004\t    but needs more work to be publishable.\n1005\t\n1006\t    '\n1007\t  tables:\n1008\t  - name: Intervention hierarchy with uncertainty gating\n1009\t    columns:\n1010\t    - Level\n1011\t    - Method\n1012\t    - Success rate\n1013\t    - Mechanism\n1014\t    rows:\n1015\t    - - 'L1: Gradient'\n1016\t      - SGS variants\n1017\t      - 1/17\n1018\t      - Backward-pass insufficient\n1019\t    - - 'L2: Output'\n1020\t      - RAVE\n1021\t      - 0/2\n1022\t      - EMA anchor polluted\n1023\t    - - 'L3: Representation'\n1024\t      - TCN\n1025\t      - 2/8\n1026\t      - Narrow dose window\n1027\t    - - 'L4: Model (new)'\n1028\t      - Uncertainty truncation\n1029\t      - 0/1 (pilot)\n1030\t      - Effective horizon reduction\n1031\t    - - Control\n1032\t      - dt_emb removal\n1033\t      - 8/8+\n1034\t      - Feature removal\n1035\t  figures_description:\n1036\t  - Truncation rate over training steps, overlaid with NVE and eval curves\n1037\t  analysis: 'Pilot 结果不够强支撑独立 claim，但为 intervention hierarchy 添加第四层。 Median 档中这会被定位为\n1038\t    \"preliminary evidence\" 放在 Discussion 中。 审稿人评价：interesting direction，please extend\n1039\t    in camera-ready。\n1040\t\n1041\t    '\n1042\t- name: Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n1043\t  plan_id: plan_040\n1044\t  description: 第三个 locomotion DMC 环境，3 configs (baseline, CIVO trigger, causal control)\n1045\t    × 3 seeds\n1046\t  expected_results:\n1047\t    baseline_mean_200K: 280\n1048\t    baseline_std: 45\n1049\t    civo_trigger_civo_rate: 2/3\n1050\t    civo_trigger_mean_nve_peak: 5.2\n1051\t    civo_trigger_mean_eval_vs_baseline: 25%\n1052\t    causal_control_civo_rate: 0/3\n1053\t    causal_control_mean_eval_vs_baseline: 35%\n1054\t    total_gpu_hours: 45\n1055\t  result_rationale: 'Hopper Hop 是比 Walker Walk 更难的 locomotion 任务（DreamerV3 baseline\n1056\t    ~250-300）。 CIVO 预计出现但环境本身的 high variance 和 lower baseline 使 NVE normalization\n1057\t    更嘈杂。 2/3 崩溃率（比 Cheetah 的 3/3 低）因为 Hopper 的 value landscape 有不同 topology。 Median\n1058\t    档审稿人：第四个环境加强了 generalization 但仍是 DMC proprioceptive setting—— \"all four environments\n1059\t    are DMC proprioceptive, how do we know this isn''t a DMC-specific artifact?\" Pixel\n1060\t    observation 的缺失仍是 core weakness (Dream D9)。 45 GPU hours 的预算对 P2 priority 可能不被分配——median\n1061\t    档假设这个实验可能不做。\n1062\t\n1063\t    '\n1064\t  tables:\n1065\t  - name: Four-environment CIVO summary\n1066\t    columns:\n1067\t    - Environment\n1068\t    - Obs dim\n1069\t    - Baseline\n1070\t    - CIVO rate\n1071\t    - Causal control rate\n1072\t    rows:\n1073\t    - - Walker Walk\n1074\t      - '24'\n1075\t      - ~950\n1076\t      - 2/4 (50%)\n1077\t      - 0/8 (0%)\n1078\t    - - Cheetah Run\n1079\t      - '17'\n1080\t      - ~600\n1081\t      - 3/3 (100%)\n1082\t      - 0/3 (0%)\n1083\t    - - Cartpole Swingup\n1084\t      - '5'\n1085\t      - ~860\n1086\t      - 3/3 (100%)\n1087\t      - 0/3 (0%)\n1088\t    - - Hopper Hop\n1089\t      - '15'\n1090\t      - ~280\n1091\t      - 2/3 (67%)\n1092\t      - 0/3 (0%)\n1093\t    - - '**Total**'\n1094\t      - —\n1095\t      - —\n1096\t      - '**10/13 (77%)**'\n1097\t      - '**0/17 (0%)**'\n1098\t  figures_description:\n1099\t  - 'Cross-environment radar chart: CIVO rate, severity, eval retention, causal control\n1100\t    effectiveness'\n1101\t  analysis: Hopper 的加入使总 CIVO detection 达 10/13（77%）和因果控制 0/17（100% prevention）。 但\n1102\t    median 档审稿人的核心攻击不在环境数量而在环境多样性： 全部 4 个都是 DMC continuous control + proprioceptive\n1103\t    observation + RSSM。 要 \"truly generalize\" 需要不同 world model（IRIS/TWM）或 pixel observation。\n1104\t    此实验在 median 档中被视为 \"nice to have\" 而非 \"changes the verdict\"。\n1105\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8160c2d3-e1f0-4475-97c0-9800d500973c","uuid":"95cc0381-82fd-4b59-aa21-79bbe5579335","timestamp":"2026-05-20T21:46:02.040Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T210241/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '部分假设未完全验证，需调整 claims 强度并补充实验。具体：(1) MPC/imagination 架构边界从 \"novel\n  finding\" 弱化为 \"empirical observation consistent with architectural dependency\"，Discussion\n  中加入 TAWM 设定差异的详细对比表（obs space / planning horizon / critic structure / dt range），明确哪些\n  confounds 未控制；(2) 梯度-因果解耦从独立贡献降级为 C7 的 supporting analysis，不在 abstract/intro 中突出；(3)\n  补充 ensemble critic 快速消融——在 DreamerV3 critic 上加 2-head ensemble + min-Q，即使简化版也堵住\n  R9 的 \"没试过标准对策\" 攻击（预计 1-2 天 GPU，2 seeds，Walker 单环境）；(4) NVE 讨论加入 leave-one-environment-out\n  cross-validation AUROC（已有 4 环境数据可离线计算）+ bootstrap 95% CI；(5) 论文标题考虑从 \"Diagnosing...\"\n  改为 \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails...\" 以降低 novelty 期望值。Rebuttal 可将 borderline 翻转但需额外\n  2-3 天实验。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 复制 008d 配置（subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8）到 seed 1 和 seed 2，验证\n    CIVO 崩溃的跨 seed 可复现性\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 131\n    seed1_nve_peak: 4.12\n    seed1_nve_peak_step: 55K\n    seed1_collapse: true\n    seed1_collapse_onset: 25K\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 268\n    seed2_nve_peak: 2.05\n    seed2_nve_peak_step: 25K\n    seed2_collapse: false\n    seed2_self_correction: true\n    seed2_nve_105K: 0.38\n    collapse_rate: 1/2 (50%)\n    nve_gt_1.5x_rate: 2/2 (100%)\n    nve_threshold_separation: 4/4 perfect (trained 2/2 > 1.5x, untrained 0/2 < 1.5x)\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档认可 nve>1.5x 阈值的 4/4 分离力作为诊断工具，但对崩溃率 50%（仅 2 个独立 seed）的统计\n    power 提出质疑。 Seed 1 重现经典 CIVO（value 爆炸 → eval 下降），seed 2 自我修正（transient nve>1.5x\n    → 回落）。 审稿人会指出：2 seeds 只能给出 50% 的点估计，95% CI 覆盖 [7%, 93%]（Clopper-Pearson），无法区分\n    \"rare event\" 和 \"coin flip\"。 这是 median 档 major weakness #1：per-method 样本量不足。Full\n    SGS 仅 3 seeds、RAVE 仅 2 configs 同样被标记。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 008d cross-seed NVE trajectory\n    columns:\n    - Step\n    - Seed 0 NVE\n    - Seed 1 NVE\n    - Seed 2 NVE\n    rows:\n    - - 25K\n      - '1.78'\n      - '1.78'\n      - '2.05'\n    - - 35K\n      - '1.71'\n      - '1.71'\n      - '1.24'\n    - - 45K\n      - '2.09'\n      - '2.09'\n      - '1.62'\n    - - 55K\n      - '4.12'\n      - '4.12'\n      - '1.41'\n    - - 65K\n      - '-'\n      - '1.23'\n      - '0.94'\n    - - 85K\n      - '-'\n      - '1.15'\n      - '0.51'\n    - - 105K\n      - '-'\n      - '1.57'\n      - '0.38'\n  figures_description:\n  - NVE 时间序列图：3 seeds 并排，标注 1.5x 阈值线。Seed 0/1 持续超阈值，seed 2 transient 后回落。\n  analysis: 'CIVO 诊断标记（nve>1.5x）具有 100% 敏感性（2/2 trained seeds 均触发），但崩溃本身是随机的。 Median\n    档审稿人接受因果方向（trained dt_emb → pathological overestimation）但质疑： (a) 仅 2 seeds 的崩溃率不具统计意义；(b)\n    self-correction 机制未解释——如果 CIVO 可以 self-correct， 为什么还需要干预？需要在 rebuttal 中强调：self-correction\n    不可靠（seed 2 eval 仅恢复到 268 = 29% baseline）， 且 sustained vs transient overestimation\n    的分界点无法事先预测。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 复制 008f 因果控制（subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8）到 seed 1-2，验证无 dt_embedding\n    时的稳定性\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 503\n    seed1_nve_105K: 0.3\n    seed1_collapse: false\n    seed1_trend: zigzag recovery 173→375→324→246→319→503\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 148\n    seed2_nve_105K: 1.14\n    seed2_collapse: false\n    seed2_trend: peak 359@75K then monotonic decline to 148\n    reward_MAE: 0.747\n    reward_MAE_vs_baseline: 75x\n    cross_seed_consistency: poor — seed 1 recovers to 503, seed 2 declines to 148\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档的关键攻击点在 008f 的 reward_MAE（baseline 的 75x）和跨 seed 不一致性。\n    Seed 1 的 zigzag recovery 到 503（55% baseline）是合理的；seed 2 declining 到 148（16% baseline）\n    则暴露 008f 不是一个可靠的 \"保护\" 方案。审稿人会问：\"如果去掉 dt_embedding 导致 reward prediction 崩塌（MAE=0.747），\n    那么 008f 的''稳定性''是否只是因为 critic 已经无法学到有意义的值——是''保护''还是''功能丧失''？\" 这个质疑在 median 档是合理的——008f\n    的定位必须严格限制在\"因果控制实验\"（证明 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件）， 不能作为推荐方案。Seed 2 的 nve=1.14x@105K（borderline）也会被拿来质疑阈值的鲁棒性。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 008f cross-seed comparison\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Seed 0 (s0)\n    - Seed 1\n    - Seed 2\n    rows:\n    - - eval@105K\n      - '503'\n      - 503*\n      - '148'\n    - - NVE@105K\n      - '0.30'\n      - 0.30*\n      - '1.14'\n    - - Peak eval\n      - 503@105K\n      - 503@105K*\n      - 359@75K\n    - - Trend\n      - zigzag recovery\n      - zigzag recovery*\n      - monotonic decline\n    note: '*seed 0 和 seed 1 实为同一 seed（deterministic reproduction），仅 seed 2 为独立 seed'\n  figures_description:\n  - 008f seed 1 vs seed 2 eval 曲线对比，标注 reward_MAE=0.747 作为功能退化警告\n  analysis: '008f 作为因果控制实验成功证明了 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件（两个 seed 均未出现 nve>1.5x），\n    但跨 seed 性能差异巨大（503 vs 148），且 reward prediction 严重退化。 Median 档审稿人至少会标记这一点为 major\n    weakness：causal control 的清洁度被 reward 退化污染。 Rebuttal 策略：承认 008f 不是方案而是诊断工具，将推荐方案指向\n    008e_v3（C6）或完全移除 dt_embedding（C7 after D107）。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: 验证 008e_v3（trained dt_emb + dt=1 imagination + subsample ON + H=15）在\n    seed 1-2 的 mitigation 效果\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 870\n    seed1_nve_105K: 0.8\n    seed1_collapse: false\n    seed1_vs_baseline: 95%\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 137\n    seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n    seed2_collapse: true\n    seed2_collapse_onset: 95K\n    seed2_mechanism: non-CIVO (eval-driven, entropy ↑, policy destabilization)\n    collapse_rate: 1/2 (50%)\n    mitigation_verdict: PARTIALLY FALSIFIED\n  result_rationale: '这是 median 档最关键的结果之一。dt=1 imagination 曾被假设为实用 mitigation（seed\n    1: 95% baseline, nve=0.80x）， 但 seed 2 崩溃否证了该假设。审稿人会抓住两点： (1) 50% 崩溃率与 008d（dt=2\n    imagination）的 50% 崩溃率相同——dt=1 imagination 未降低崩溃概率； (2) seed 2 的崩溃机制（entropy 上升、eval\n    先跌、value 温和变化）与经典 CIVO 定性不同， 说明 trained dt_embedding 通过多条路径创造脆弱性。 Median 档审稿人认为这是\n    \"interesting observation\"（多路径脆弱性），但不够强——仅 2 seeds， 且两种崩溃机制的区分缺乏正式统计检验。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 008e_v3 collapse dynamics comparison\n    columns:\n    - Feature\n    - Seed 1 (healthy)\n    - Seed 2 (collapsed)\n    - 008d s0 (classic CIVO)\n    rows:\n    - - eval@105K\n      - 870 (95% baseline)\n      - 137 (15% baseline)\n      - 83 (9% baseline)\n    - - NVE@105K\n      - '0.80'\n      - '3.78'\n      - '4.12'\n    - - Value trajectory\n      - monotonically rising\n      - 339→384→340 (±13%)\n      - 25→60→98→138 (+130%)\n    - - Entropy@collapse\n      - -5.2 (stable)\n      - -5.2→-3.8 (rising)\n      - -3.5→-4.9 (falling)\n    - - Collapse driver\n      - N/A\n      - eval crash → NVE spike\n      - value explosion → eval drop\n    - - Pathway\n      - —\n      - B (IRD, policy instability)\n      - A (CIVO, value-driven)\n  figures_description:\n  - '3 panel figure: seed 1 healthy trajectory, seed 2 collapse with entropy annotation,\n    008d classic CIVO for contrast'\n  analysis: 'C6 partially falsified 是论文的重要转折点——从 \"practical mitigation\" 转为 \"diagnostic\n    evidence\"。 Median 档的 narrative 建议是将此发现框架为 \"trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability\n    through multiple pathways\"， 但审稿人会认为 2 seeds 不足以可靠区分两种 pathway。 额外 seeds (plan_016)\n    的 2/4 崩溃率确认了 50% 但仍不足以做正式统计——median 档要求至少 6-8 seeds per config。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 验证 008a（subsample OFF + unexposed trained dt_emb + H=15）的值抑制和 V-recovery\n    模式\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 631\n    seed1_nve_105K: 0.43\n    seed1_civo_alert: 0\n    seed1_trend: gradual rise 140→394→414→441→492→453→547→629→631\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 899\n    seed2_nve_105K: 0.33\n    seed2_civo_alert: 0\n    seed2_trend: faster convergence 311→432→608→654→534→605→819→899\n    cross_seed_mean_105K: 770\n    cross_seed_std: 137\n    vs_baseline_mean: 84%\n    nve_range_all_seeds: 0.33-0.93\n  result_rationale: 'Unexposed trained dt_emb（subsample OFF 意味着 dt_emb 从未见过 dt>1 数据）应表现类似\n    untrained dt_emb： NVE 抑制 + 无 CIVO。Seed 0 (778@105K)、seed 1 (631)、seed 2 (899)\n    均无崩溃，NVE 全程 < 1.0x。 但跨 seed 方差大（631-899, CV≈18%），median 档审稿人会指出：(a) 3 seeds 的均值\n    770±137 只能说 \"大致恢复\"， precision 不够；(b) 008a 的 zigzag pattern 是 DreamerV3 的一般特征还是特定于此配置？\n    缺乏 baseline 同 seed 对照的 zigzag 频率对比。这不会是 major weakness 但会被标注。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 008a cross-seed summary\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Seed 0\n    - Seed 1\n    - Seed 2\n    - Mean ± Std\n    rows:\n    - - eval@105K\n      - '778'\n      - '631'\n      - '899'\n      - 770 ± 137\n    - - NVE@105K\n      - '0.59'\n      - '0.43'\n      - '0.33'\n      - 0.45 ± 0.13\n    - - Peak eval\n      - 778@105K\n      - 631@105K\n      - 899@105K\n      - —\n    - - vs baseline\n      - 85%\n      - 69%\n      - 98%\n      - 84% ± 15%\n    - - CIVO alert\n      - '0'\n      - '0'\n      - '0'\n      - 0/3\n  figures_description:\n  - 008a 3-seed eval learning curves with IQM band, overlaid with baseline for reference\n  analysis: 'C3（untrained/unexposed dt_emb 保护）在 3 seeds 中全部确认：NVE 持续 <1.0x，无 CIVO。\n    Median 档接受 C3 的因果方向但认为 84% baseline recovery 不够有说服力—— \"如果最优 mitigation 还是损失 16%\n    performance，这更像是 ''less bad'' 而不是 ''solution''\"。 审稿人建议与完全移除 dt_emb 的 008f 对比成本效益。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: 扩展 008e_v3 到 seed 3-4，缩窄崩溃概率估计的置信区间\n  expected_results:\n    seed3_eval_return_105K: 93\n    seed3_nve_peak: 4.02\n    seed3_collapse: true\n    seed3_collapse_onset: 85K-95K\n    seed3_entropy_signature: -4.89 (falling — closer to Pathway A/CIVO)\n    seed4_eval_return_105K: 899\n    seed4_nve_peak: 0.99\n    seed4_collapse: false\n    collapse_rate_4seeds: 2/4 (50%)\n    collapse_95CI: '[7%, 93%] (Clopper-Pearson exact)'\n  result_rationale: '4 seeds 中 2 个崩溃（s2 和 s3）、2 个存活（s1 和 s4），确认 50% 崩溃率的点估计。 但 Clopper-Pearson\n    95% CI 仍为 [7%, 93%]，审稿人正确指出这个区间太宽，无法做有意义的推断。 Seed 3 的崩溃（entropy 下降）看起来更接近 Pathway\n    A（CIVO），而 seed 2（entropy 上升）是 Pathway B（IRD）， 但 n=2 per pathway 完全不够做统计区分。 Median\n    档的核心批评：50% 崩溃率意味着 dt=1 imagination 和 dt=2 imagination 的脆弱性相同， 那么 \"架构边界\" 叙事的增量价值在哪里？\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 008e_v3 all-seed collapse summary\n    columns:\n    - Seed\n    - eval@105K\n    - NVE peak\n    - Collapse?\n    - Pathway\n    rows:\n    - - s1\n      - '870'\n      - '0.80'\n      - 'No'\n      - —\n    - - s2\n      - '137'\n      - '3.78'\n      - 'Yes'\n      - B (IRD, entropy ↑)\n    - - s3\n      - '93'\n      - '4.02'\n      - 'Yes'\n      - A-like (entropy ↓)\n    - - s4\n      - '899'\n      - '0.99'\n      - 'No'\n      - —\n    - - Rate\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 2/4 = 50%\n      - Mixed\n  figures_description:\n  - 4-seed eval trajectory panel with collapse onset markers, color-coded by pathway\n    type\n  analysis: 'Plan_016 的 4 seeds 收窄了估计但统计力仍不足。Median 档审稿人会标记： \"4 seeds per config ×\n    50% collapse rate = 单位实验成本下统计效率极低， 需要 ≥12 seeds 才能将 CI 缩窄到有意义区间 [30%, 70%]。\" 对\n    rebuttal 价值有限——确认了 50% 但无法 defend against \"statistically underpowered\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: freeze dt_embedding（requires_grad=False），保持随机初始化。诊断 dt_emb 的 TRAINING\n    是否是 CIVO 的必要条件\n  expected_results:\n    eval_return_105K: 204\n    nve_105K: 0.42\n    nve_range: 0.39-0.47\n    collapse: false\n    actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n    actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n    value_mean_105K: 56.2\n    gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n    failure_mode: gradient_starvation — actor_loss→0, critic underestimates\n    vs_baseline: 22%\n  result_rationale: 'Frozen dt_emb 阻止了 CIVO（NVE 0.39-0.47，远低于 1.5x），确认了 dt_emb TRAINING\n    是 CIVO 的必要条件。 但引入了新失败模式：gradient starvation。随机初始化的 frozen embedding 给 RSSM 提供无信息量的\n    conditioning signal， actor_loss→0 意味着 actor 梯度消失，策略无法有效改进。 Median 档审稿人会认为这是 \"expected\n    but useful\"——frozen random embedding 当然不好用， 但它闭合了 2×2 消融矩阵（trained/frozen × exposed/unexposed）。\n    Novelty 评价：2.5-3.0。这个结果是消融设计的自然推论，不是独立贡献。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: dt_emb training ablation matrix\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - Exposed to dt>1 (subsample ON)\n    - Unexposed (subsample OFF)\n    rows:\n    - - Trained dt_emb\n      - '008d: CIVO collapse (NVE 2.09x)'\n      - '008a: V-recovery (NVE 0.59x)'\n    - - Frozen dt_emb\n      - '015b: gradient starvation (NVE 0.42x)'\n      - (= 008a equivalent, cancelled)\n    - - No dt_emb (dim=0)\n      - '008f: reward degradation (NVE 0.30x)'\n      - N/A\n  figures_description:\n  - 2×2 消融矩阵热力图：NVE peak × eval@105K，标注每个 cell 的失败模式\n  analysis: '015b 闭合了关键消融，但 median 档审稿人会指出矩阵的解读过度简化： 仅 1 seed per cell（除 008d 有多 seed），且不同\n    cell 的失败模式（CIVO vs gradient starvation vs reward degradation） 不可比——不能简单用 NVE 一个指标统一评估。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_020\n  description: Cheetah Run dt=1 baseline，建立第二环境的 v/e calibration\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_200K: 625\n    seed1_eval_return_200K: 520\n    seed2_eval_return_200K: 645\n    cross_seed_mean: 597\n    cross_seed_std: 68\n    ve_ratio_converged: 0.60-0.70\n    convergence_step: 150K-200K\n  result_rationale: 'Cheetah Run baseline 表现低于 Walker Walk（~600 vs ~950），variance\n    更高。 已有 5 seeds 数据（s0=625, s1=520, s2=645, s3=642, s4=537），均值 594±54。 Median 档审稿人接受\n    baseline 稳定性但会注意到 s4 的 194K→204K 骤降（537→302 transient drop）， 质疑 Cheetah 基线本身的不稳定性是否混淆了\n    CIVO 诊断。 Converged v/e 约 0.60-0.70，为 NVE normalization 提供基准。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cheetah baseline cross-seed\n    columns:\n    - Seed\n    - eval_final\n    - eval_peak\n    - ve_ratio_converged\n    rows:\n    - - s0\n      - '625'\n      - '625'\n      - ~0.65\n    - - s1\n      - '520'\n      - '573'\n      - ~0.60\n    - - s2\n      - '645'\n      - '645'\n      - ~0.65\n    - - Mean\n      - '597'\n      - '614'\n      - ~0.63\n  figures_description:\n  - Cheetah baseline 3-seed learning curves with IQM confidence band\n  analysis: 'Baseline 确立但 inter-seed variance（CV≈11%）高于 Walker（CV≈3%）， 这意味着 Cheetah\n    的 CIVO 检测需要更多 seeds 才能达到 Walker 的统计 power。 Median 档审稿人会指出此 asymmetry。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_021\n  description: Cheetah Run 中复制 CIVO trigger（dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb）\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_105K: 1\n    seed0_nve_peak: 70.64\n    seed0_civo: true\n    seed0_collapse_type: catastrophic\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 52\n    seed1_nve_peak: 8.27\n    seed1_civo: true\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 85\n    seed2_nve_peak: 12.5\n    seed2_civo: true\n    civo_rate: 3/3 (100%)\n    mean_nve_peak: 30.5\n    cheetah_vs_walker_severity: Cheetah CIVO severity >> Walker (mean NVE 30x vs 3x)\n  result_rationale: 'Cheetah 已有 2 seeds 数据（s0: NVE=70.64 catastrophic, s1/exp_010b:\n    NVE=8.27 severe）。 Cheetah 的 CIVO 比 Walker 严重得多——NVE 峰值 8-70x vs Walker 的 2-4x。\n    这是因为 Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 更大（更高维运动学 → dt>1 预测更难）。 预测 seed 2 也会 CIVO（NVE\n    ~10-15x），给出 3/3 = 100% 崩溃率。 Median 档认为这强化了 C1/C2 的跨环境泛化，但会质疑： (a) Cheetah 的 CIVO\n    动力学与 Walker 定性不同（更早、更严重），是否真是同一机制？ (b) 仅 2 个环境（Walker + Cheetah）不够 claim \"generalizes\"——3\n    环境是最低限度。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cheetah CIVO trigger cross-seed\n    columns:\n    - Seed\n    - eval@105K\n    - NVE peak\n    - Collapse type\n    rows:\n    - - s0\n      - ~1\n      - '70.64'\n      - catastrophic\n    - - s1\n      - '52'\n      - '8.27'\n      - severe\n    - - s2 (predicted)\n      - ~85\n      - ~12.5\n      - severe\n  figures_description:\n  - Cheetah NVE time series 3 seeds vs Walker 3 seeds, showing environment-dependent\n    severity\n  analysis: 'Cheetah 的 100% 崩溃率（vs Walker 50%）和更高 NVE 峰值是双刃剑： 强化了 CIVO 是真实威胁，但也暗示\n    Walker 的 50% 可能是偏低的 — 环境越难 CIVO 越强。 Median 档审稿人接受跨环境 CIVO 存在性但认为 severity 差异（10x）需要解释：\n    是 RSSM capacity 差异还是 task complexity 差异？\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_022\n  description: Cheetah Run 因果控制：去掉 dt_embedding 是否阻止 CIVO\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_105K: 97\n    seed0_nve_peak: 0.2\n    seed0_civo: false\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 77\n    seed1_nve_peak: 0.1\n    seed1_civo: false\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 90\n    seed2_nve_peak: 0.15\n    seed2_civo: false\n    civo_prevention_rate: 3/3 (100%)\n    mean_eval_vs_baseline: 15%\n    reward_MAE_vs_baseline: '>50x'\n  result_rationale: '已有 2 seeds：s0 eval=96.5（NVE 0.2, no CIVO），s1 eval=77.3（NVE 0.1,\n    no CIVO）。 与 Walker 008f 一致：去掉 dt_embedding 完全阻止 CIVO，但 eval 严重退化（仅 ~15% baseline）。\n    Cheetah 的退化比 Walker 更严重（Walker 008f 达 55% baseline），因为 Cheetah 对 reward prediction\n    更敏感。 Median 档接受因果控制成立（5/5 across 2 environments: no dt_emb → no CIVO）， 但再次质疑：这是\n    \"prevention\" 还是 \"feature removal leading to functional impairment\"？\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cross-environment causal control (dt_embed_dim=0)\n    columns:\n    - Environment\n    - Seeds\n    - CIVO rate\n    - Mean eval vs baseline\n    - Reward MAE ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Walker Walk\n      - 3 (s0, s3, s4)\n      - 0/3\n      - ~40%\n      - 75x\n    - - Cheetah Run\n      - 2-3\n      - 0/3\n      - ~15%\n      - '>50x'\n    - - Combined\n      - 5-6\n      - 0/5+\n      - ~30%\n      - '>>1x'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: CIVO rate and eval retention for dt_embed_dim=0 across environments'\n  analysis: '因果控制在 Cheetah 中复现，5/5 完美分离确认 dt_embedding 是 CIVO 的必要条件。 但 eval 退化在 Cheetah\n    更严重，暴露了一个 tension：去掉 dt_embedding \"治愈\" CIVO 但也移除了 dt-conditioning 的功能价值。这对 \"CIVO\n    是 dt-conditioning 不可避免的副作用\" 的叙事有利， 但审稿人会要求解释为什么不能 have both（有效 conditioning +\n    无 CIVO）。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_023\n  description: Cheetah Run 中验证 unexposed trained dt_emb 的值抑制效果\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_105K: 532\n    seed0_nve_105K: 0.49\n    seed0_civo: false\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 504\n    seed1_nve_105K: 0.48\n    seed1_civo: false\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 480\n    seed2_nve_105K: 0.52\n    seed2_civo: false\n    mean_eval_vs_baseline: 85%\n    nve_range: 0.48-0.52\n  result_rationale: '已有 2 seeds：s0=532（NVE 0.49），s1=504（NVE 0.48）。Unexposed dt_emb\n    在 Cheetah 中也有效： NVE < 1.0x，eval 保留 ~85% baseline。与 Walker 008a 一致（84% baseline）。\n    这是 C3 跨环境验证的最强数据：两个环境的 unexposed dt_emb 均表现出值抑制 + 高 eval 保留。 Median 档接受 C3 但认为\n    \"unexposed = subsample OFF\" 只是一种 workaround， 不是对 CIVO 机制的根本解决。\"如果你不让模型见到 dt>1\n    数据，当然不会 CIVO——但这也失去了 temporal abstraction 的目的。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'C3 cross-environment: unexposed dt_emb'\n    columns:\n    - Environment\n    - Seeds\n    - Mean eval vs baseline\n    - NVE range\n    - CIVO\n    rows:\n    - - Walker Walk\n      - '3'\n      - 84%\n      - 0.33-0.93\n      - 0/3\n    - - Cheetah Run\n      - 2-3\n      - 85%\n      - 0.48-0.52\n      - 0/3\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cross-environment eval retention bar chart: unexposed dt_emb vs baseline vs trained\n    dt_emb'\n  analysis: 'C3 获得跨环境确认（6 seeds, 0 CIVO, 84-85% baseline），是论文中最 robust 的正面结果。 但 median\n    档正确指出这不是 mitigation——它避开了问题而非解决问题。\n\n    '\n- name: 'RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions'\n  plan_id: plan_030\n  description: 量化不同模型在 dt=1 和 dt=2 上的 RSSM 预测质量差距\n  expected_results:\n    baseline_obs_gap: 2.04\n    baseline_reward_gap: 1.56\n    008d_obs_gap: 1.3\n    008d_reward_gap: 2.78\n    008f_obs_gap: 2.75\n    008f_reward_gap: 1.01\n    008d_dt1_obs_MSE: 41.31\n    baseline_dt1_obs_MSE: 13.49\n    key_finding: 008d 的低 obs gap (1.30x) 具误导性——其 dt=1 绝对误差已是 baseline 3x\n  result_rationale: 'RSSM fidelity 分析已完成（exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis）。核心发现： 008d 的\n    obs gap ratio 看起来最小（1.30x），但绝对误差最大（dt1: 41.31 vs baseline 13.49）， 说明模型整体已崩塌，gap\n    ratio 失去意义。008f 的 reward gap (1.01x) 说明无 dt_embedding 时 reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2——这是\n    \"功能丧失\" 不是 \"改善\"。 Median 档审稿人认为这是 \"expected and confirmatory\"——RSSM 在 dt>1 预测不好是已知的，\n    novelty 不在发现本身而在它与 CIVO 的因果连接。但审稿人会质疑： 只有 1 个 checkpoint 的分析，如何确认这是训练全程的 pattern\n    而非特定 step 的 artifact？\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: RSSM Fidelity Table\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - dt1 obs_MSE\n    - dt2 obs_MSE\n    - obs gap\n    - dt1 reward_MAE\n    - dt2 reward_MAE\n    - reward gap\n    rows:\n    - - baseline\n      - '13.49'\n      - '27.50'\n      - 2.04x\n      - '0.0102'\n      - '0.0159'\n      - 1.56x\n    - - 008d (trained dt_emb)\n      - '41.31'\n      - '53.67'\n      - 1.30x\n      - '0.0568'\n      - '0.1579'\n      - 2.78x\n    - - 008f (no dt_emb)\n      - '8.01'\n      - '22.04'\n      - 2.75x\n      - '0.7469'\n      - '0.7526'\n      - 1.01x\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart with both absolute values and ratios side-by-side, preventing ratio-only\n    misleading\n  analysis: 'RSSM fidelity 分析确认了机制假说但未超越 \"supporting evidence\"。 Median 档给这个分析 moderate\n    credit 但不视为独立贡献。 建议在 rebuttal 中加入训练过程中 fidelity 的演化曲线（多 checkpoint），回应 \"single\n    snapshot\" 质疑。\n\n    '\n- name: Actor entropy analysis\n  plan_id: plan_031\n  description: 对比健康 vs 崩溃配置的 actor entropy 演化\n  expected_results:\n    healthy_008a_entropy_trend: 稳定在 -4.5 to -5.2 范围\n    healthy_008c_entropy_trend: 缓慢下降 -3.5 → -4.8\n    collapsed_006_entropy_trend: 下降后回弹 -3.5 → -4.9 → -3.8\n    collapsed_008d_entropy_trend: 持续下降 -1.9 → -4.9\n    collapsed_008e_v3_s2_entropy_trend: 先降后升 -5.2 → -3.8 (反常)\n    pathway_A_signature: entropy ↓ (policy 过度确定化)\n    pathway_B_signature: entropy ↑ (policy destabilization)\n  result_rationale: 'Actor entropy 分析是区分 Pathway A (CIVO) 和 Pathway B (IRD) 的关键诊断工具。\n    经典 CIVO (008d): value overestimate → actor exploit → entropy 下降 → 策略变得过度确定。 非\n    CIVO 崩溃 (008e_v3_s2): eval 先跌 → value 滞后 → entropy 上升 → 策略变得随机。 Median 档认为这是 \"useful\n    characterization\" 但不是 \"novel contribution\"—— entropy 作为策略健康度指标是标准做法，两种 pathway\n    的区分缺乏 formal framework。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Entropy trajectory comparison\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Entropy@35K\n    - Entropy@55K\n    - Entropy@85K\n    - Entropy@105K\n    - Pathway\n    rows:\n    - - 008a s0 (healthy)\n      - '-4.2'\n      - '-4.5'\n      - '-4.8'\n      - '-5.0'\n      - —\n    - - 008d s0 (CIVO)\n      - '-3.5'\n      - '-4.9'\n      - —\n      - —\n      - A\n    - - 008e_v3 s2 (IRD)\n      - '-3.5'\n      - '-5.1'\n      - '-5.2'\n      - '-3.8'\n      - B\n    - - 016e (SGS)\n      - '-2.1'\n      - '-3.6'\n      - '-4.3'\n      - —\n      - A (delayed)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Entropy vs step: healthy configs (blue band) vs CIVO (red, entropy ↓) vs IRD\n    (orange, entropy ↑)'\n  analysis: 'Entropy 分析确认两种崩溃 pathway 的存在，但 n=1-2 per pathway 不足以 formalize。 Median\n    档审稿人建议：如果要将 dual-pathway 作为贡献，需要至少 5 seeds per pathway 并做 statistical test。\n\n    '\n- name: Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\n  plan_id: plan_032\n  description: V(s) vs Monte Carlo return 分布对比\n  expected_results:\n    trained_dt_emb_divergence: V(s) 分布右偏移 + 重尾，MC return 集中在低区间\n    untrained_dt_emb_match: V(s) 和 MC return 分布大致重叠，V(s) 略微左移\n    collapsed_state: V(s) 均值远超 MC return p95，完全脱钩\n    healthy_calibration: V(s) 中位数在 MC return IQR 内\n  result_rationale: '这是对 v/e ratio proxy 的补充验证。直接展示 V(s) 分布 vs 实际回报分布比单一 ratio 更具信息量。\n    Median 档审稿人在 R3 中质疑 v/e ratio 是 crude proxy——这个分析直接回应。 预期结果：trained dt_emb 的 V(s)\n    明显偏高且扩散，untrained 的则接近校准。 但审稿人仍会指出：MC return 在 imagination 中不可直接计算（需要 ground truth\n    environment）， 只能用 eval return 作为 proxy，引入额外近似误差。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - '2×2 violin plot panel: (trained/untrained) × (pre-collapse/post-collapse), V(s)\n    distribution in orange vs MC return in blue'\n  analysis: 'Distributional 分析增加了 R3 的防御深度，但实现依赖 eval return 作为 MC return proxy， 审稿人可能认为这只是换了一种方式展示同样的信息。Median\n    档给 minor positive credit。\n\n    '\n- name: dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\n  plan_id: plan_033\n  description: 分析 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 向量的演化\n  expected_results:\n    initial_cosine_sim: ~0.0 (random init)\n    trained_25K_cosine_sim: ~0.3\n    trained_55K_cosine_sim: ~0.65\n    trained_105K_cosine_sim: ~0.75 (converging)\n    l2_distance_trend: monotonically increasing\n    frozen_cosine_sim: constant at ~0.0\n  result_rationale: 'Trained dt_embedding 的 dt=1 和 dt=2 向量会在训练过程中逐渐分离（cosine sim 从\n    ~0 增加， 但 L2 距离增加），说明 embedding 学到了 dt-specific representation。 Frozen embedding\n    保持初始状态不变（cosine sim ≈ 0）。 Median 档认为这是 \"descriptive visualization\"——确认 embedding\n    在训练，但不提供超越已知的 insight。 审稿人的反应：nice plot, but what does it tell us that we didn''t\n    already know from the gradient analysis?\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2 embedding vectors over training\n    steps, for trained vs frozen'\n  analysis: 'Low priority（P2）合理。Cosine similarity 分析提供视觉直觉但不支撑任何独立 claim。 Median 档中这会出现在\n    appendix 如果提交，不会影响评分。\n\n    '\n- name: NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\n  plan_id: plan_034\n  description: 在不同阈值（1.3x, 1.5x, 1.7x, 2.0x）下计算分类准确率和 AUROC\n  expected_results:\n    threshold_1.3x_accuracy: 0.86\n    threshold_1.5x_accuracy: 0.93\n    threshold_1.7x_accuracy: 0.9\n    threshold_2.0x_accuracy: 0.83\n    youden_optimal_threshold: 1.53\n    AUROC_walker: 0.98\n    AUROC_cheetah: 0.95\n    AUROC_combined: 0.969\n    AUROC_bootstrap_95CI: '[0.91, 1.00]'\n    n_total_datapoints: 29\n    leave_one_env_out_AUROC_walker_train: 0.97\n    leave_one_env_out_AUROC_cheetah_test: 0.92\n  result_rationale: 'NVE 阈值分析基于所有可用 seeds（~29 数据点跨 4 环境）。1.5x 是 near-optimal（Youden\n    index 收敛到 1.53x）， AUROC 0.969 表明 NVE 是 strong discriminator。 但 median 档审稿人一致标记（Dream\n    D8）：阈值在同数据集上 calibrate 和 validate = in-sample bias。 Leave-one-environment-out\n    CV 部分回应这个问题（Cheetah 作为 held-out 时 AUROC 仍 ~0.92）， 但只有 2 个环境做 LOO-CV 统计意义有限。 Bootstrap\n    95% CI [0.91, 1.00] 看起来 impressive 但样本量小时 bootstrap CI 本身偏乐观。 这是 median 档的核心方法论弱点之一。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: NVE threshold ROC analysis\n    columns:\n    - Threshold\n    - Sensitivity\n    - Specificity\n    - Accuracy\n    - Youden J\n    rows:\n    - - 1.3x\n      - '0.94'\n      - '0.80'\n      - '0.86'\n      - '0.74'\n    - - 1.5x\n      - '0.88'\n      - '1.00'\n      - '0.93'\n      - '0.88'\n    - - 1.53x (optimal)\n      - '0.88'\n      - '1.00'\n      - '0.93'\n      - '0.88'\n    - - 1.7x\n      - '0.81'\n      - '1.00'\n      - '0.90'\n      - '0.81'\n    - - 2.0x\n      - '0.69'\n      - '1.00'\n      - '0.83'\n      - '0.69'\n  - name: Leave-one-environment-out AUROC\n    columns:\n    - Train env\n    - Test env\n    - AUROC\n    rows:\n    - - Walker\n      - Cheetah\n      - '0.92'\n    - - Cheetah\n      - Walker\n      - '0.97'\n    - - Combined\n      - Combined (bootstrap)\n      - 0.969 [0.91, 1.00]\n  figures_description:\n  - ROC curve with 95% bootstrap CI band, marking Youden-optimal threshold\n  analysis: 'AUROC 0.969 是 C2 的最强定量结果，但 in-sample calibration 和 n=29 是不可回避的限制。 Median\n    档审稿人接受 NVE 作为 diagnostic tool 但不接受 1.5x 作为 generalizable threshold。 Rebuttal 策略：承认\n    limitation，强调 leave-one-env-out 结果（虽然 n 小但方向正确）， 将 NVE threshold generalization\n    定位为 future work。\n\n    '\n- name: Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_050\n  description: 第三个 DMC 环境的 dt=1 baseline，扩展到非 locomotion 任务\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_500K: 860\n    seed1_eval_return_500K: 845\n    seed2_eval_return_500K: 870\n    cross_seed_mean: 858\n    cross_seed_std: 13\n    ve_ratio_converged: 0.65-0.75\n    convergence_step: 80K-120K\n  result_rationale: 'Cartpole Swingup 是 DMC 中相对简单的任务，DreamerV3 baseline 应快速收敛到 ~850-870。\n    Inter-seed variance 预计低于 Cheetah（simpler dynamics → more consistent learning）。\n    v/e ratio 收敛到 0.65-0.75，与 Walker/Cheetah 一致。 Median 档审稿人认为加入第三个环境是正面的（从 \"minimum\n    viable\" 的 3 环境升级）， 但 Cartpole 作为相对简单任务可能不够挑战性——\"如果 CIVO 在简单任务上弱或不出现， 这削弱了 generalization\n    claim 而非加强。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cartpole baseline\n    columns:\n    - Seed\n    - eval@500K\n    - ve_ratio_converged\n    - convergence_step\n    rows:\n    - - s0\n      - '860'\n      - '0.70'\n      - 100K\n    - - s1\n      - '845'\n      - '0.68'\n      - 110K\n    - - s2\n      - '870'\n      - '0.72'\n      - 90K\n  figures_description:\n  - Cartpole baseline learning curves, 3 seeds with confidence band\n  analysis: 'Baseline 稳定。关键问题是 CIVO 在 Cartpole 的表现——如果弱于 Walker/Cheetah， 会被解读为 \"CIVO\n    severity is task-dependent\"（median 档认可的弱化叙事）。\n\n    '\n- name: Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_051\n  description: Cartpole Swingup 中复制 CIVO trigger\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_105K: 520\n    seed0_nve_peak: 2.8\n    seed0_civo: true\n    seed0_collapse_type: partial — degradation without catastrophic collapse\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 680\n    seed1_nve_peak: 1.8\n    seed1_civo: true\n    seed1_collapse_type: mild — NVE borderline, eval recovers\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 350\n    seed2_nve_peak: 4.1\n    seed2_civo: true\n    seed2_collapse_type: moderate — sustained degradation\n    civo_rate: 3/3 (NVE > 1.5x)\n    catastrophic_collapse_rate: 0/3 (no complete collapse to random policy)\n    mean_eval_vs_baseline: 60%\n  result_rationale: 'Cartpole 比 Cheetah 简单但比 Walker 的 observation space 更低维（5 vs 24\n    dim）， RSSM 在 dt>1 的预测误差相对较小。预期 CIVO 出现（NVE > 1.5x）但严重程度低于 Walker/Cheetah： degradation\n    而非 catastrophic collapse。这是因为 Cartpole 的值函数 landscape 更平滑， value overestimation\n    更容易被 self-correction 机制缓解。 Median 档审稿人会抓住这一点：\"CIVO severity 与任务复杂度相关——在简单任务上是\n    nuisance， 在复杂任务上才是 fatal。这限制了 diagnostic 的实际影响力。\" 但也会认可：CIVO 在所有 3 个环境中都出现（NVE\n    > 1.5x），direction 一致。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cross-environment CIVO severity\n    columns:\n    - Environment\n    - CIVO rate\n    - Mean NVE peak\n    - Catastrophic collapse rate\n    - Mean eval retention\n    rows:\n    - - Walker Walk\n      - 2/4 (50%)\n      - '2.7'\n      - 2/4\n      - 47%\n    - - Cheetah Run\n      - 3/3 (100%)\n      - '30.5'\n      - 2/3\n      - 5%\n    - - Cartpole Swingup\n      - 3/3 (100%)\n      - '2.9'\n      - 0/3\n      - 60%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cross-environment CIVO heatmap: environment × seed, colored by NVE peak'\n  analysis: 'Cartpole 确认 CIVO 的 universality 但暴露了 severity 的强环境依赖性。 Median 档审稿人将此解读为\n    \"the phenomenon is real but its practical impact is task-dependent\"， 进一步将 novelty\n    定位为 incremental observation 而非 general finding。 NVE 阈值 1.5x 在 Cartpole 中仍有效（3/3\n    detection），增强了跨环境泛化的证据。\n\n    '\n- name: Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_052\n  description: Cartpole Swingup 因果控制（无 dt_embedding）\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_105K: 650\n    seed0_nve_peak: 0.35\n    seed0_civo: false\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 620\n    seed1_nve_peak: 0.4\n    seed1_civo: false\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 660\n    seed2_nve_peak: 0.3\n    seed2_civo: false\n    civo_prevention_rate: 3/3 (100%)\n    mean_eval_vs_baseline: 75%\n    reward_MAE_vs_baseline: ~30x\n  result_rationale: '无 dt_embedding 应阻止 CIVO（与 Walker/Cheetah 一致）。Cartpole 的 eval\n    保留（75%） 介于 Walker（40-55%）和 baseline 之间，因为 Cartpole 的 reward 结构更简单， reward prediction\n    退化的影响相对较小。 Median 档审稿人：因果控制在第三个环境确认，累计 8/8 across 3 environments（no dt_emb → no\n    CIVO）。 这是论文中最 robust 的因果结论之一。 但评论：\"因果控制只证明 dt_embedding 是 necessary condition，没有提供\n    mitigation pathway。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cross-environment causal control summary (final)\n    columns:\n    - Environment\n    - Seeds\n    - CIVO prevented\n    - Eval retention\n    - Reward degradation\n    rows:\n    - - Walker Walk\n      - '3'\n      - 3/3\n      - 40-55%\n      - 75x MAE\n    - - Cheetah Run\n      - 2-3\n      - 2-3/2-3\n      - ~15%\n      - '>50x MAE'\n    - - Cartpole Swingup\n      - '3'\n      - 3/3\n      - ~75%\n      - ~30x MAE\n    - - '**Total**'\n      - '**8-9**'\n      - '**8-9/8-9**'\n      - '**varies**'\n      - '**>>1x**'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar chart: eval retention by environment for dt_embed_dim=0'\n  analysis: '8/8+ 因果控制是 C2 的最终定量支撑。但 eval retention 的环境依赖性（15%-75%） 意味着 \"removing\n    dt_embedding\" 的代价不一致，进一步说明 CIVO 问题没有 one-size-fits-all solution。\n\n    '\n- name: Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\n  plan_id: plan_060\n  description: 监控 imagination rollout 中的 RSSM 预测不确定性，超过阈值时截断\n  expected_results:\n    eval_return_105K: 380\n    nve_peak: 1.8\n    civo_delayed: true\n    civo_prevented: false\n    truncation_rate_avg: 40% of rollout steps truncated\n    effective_horizon: H_eff ≈ 9 (from H=15)\n    eval_vs_baseline: 41%\n    eval_vs_008d: 2.7x better than 008d collapse\n  result_rationale: 'Uncertainty-gated truncation 在概念上是对的（截断不确定预测避免 error compounding），\n    但在 DreamerV3 的 RSSM 中面临两个问题： (1) RSSM 的 posterior entropy 不是 calibrated 的 uncertainty\n    estimate—— 高 entropy 可能反映 genuine uncertainty 也可能反映 poor representation； (2) 截断降低了\n    effective horizon，相当于变相回到 H=8 的配置（已知性能较差）。 预测结果：CIVO 延迟但不完全阻止（NVE 仍达 1.8x），eval\n    中等（380 ≈ 41% baseline）。 Median 档审稿人：interesting pilot 但 1 seed 不足以 draw conclusions。\n    This could strengthen the intervention hierarchy as a 4th level (model-level gating)\n    but needs more work to be publishable.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Intervention hierarchy with uncertainty gating\n    columns:\n    - Level\n    - Method\n    - Success rate\n    - Mechanism\n    rows:\n    - - 'L1: Gradient'\n      - SGS variants\n      - 1/17\n      - Backward-pass insufficient\n    - - 'L2: Output'\n      - RAVE\n      - 0/2\n      - EMA anchor polluted\n    - - 'L3: Representation'\n      - TCN\n      - 2/8\n      - Narrow dose window\n    - - 'L4: Model (new)'\n      - Uncertainty truncation\n      - 0/1 (pilot)\n      - Effective horizon reduction\n    - - Control\n      - dt_emb removal\n      - 8/8+\n      - Feature removal\n  figures_description:\n  - Truncation rate over training steps, overlaid with NVE and eval curves\n  analysis: 'Pilot 结果不够强支撑独立 claim，但为 intervention hierarchy 添加第四层。 Median 档中这会被定位为\n    \"preliminary evidence\" 放在 Discussion 中。 审稿人评价：interesting direction，please extend\n    in camera-ready。\n\n    '\n- name: Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n  plan_id: plan_040\n  description: 第三个 locomotion DMC 环境，3 configs (baseline, CIVO trigger, causal control)\n    × 3 seeds\n  expected_results:\n    baseline_mean_200K: 280\n    baseline_std: 45\n    civo_trigger_civo_rate: 2/3\n    civo_trigger_mean_nve_peak: 5.2\n    civo_trigger_mean_eval_vs_baseline: 25%\n    causal_control_civo_rate: 0/3\n    causal_control_mean_eval_vs_baseline: 35%\n    total_gpu_hours: 45\n  result_rationale: 'Hopper Hop 是比 Walker Walk 更难的 locomotion 任务（DreamerV3 baseline\n    ~250-300）。 CIVO 预计出现但环境本身的 high variance 和 lower baseline 使 NVE normalization\n    更嘈杂。 2/3 崩溃率（比 Cheetah 的 3/3 低）因为 Hopper 的 value landscape 有不同 topology。 Median\n    档审稿人：第四个环境加强了 generalization 但仍是 DMC proprioceptive setting—— \"all four environments\n    are DMC proprioceptive, how do we know this isn''t a DMC-specific artifact?\" Pixel\n    observation 的缺失仍是 core weakness (Dream D9)。 45 GPU hours 的预算对 P2 priority 可能不被分配——median\n    档假设这个实验可能不做。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Four-environment CIVO summary\n    columns:\n    - Environment\n    - Obs dim\n    - Baseline\n    - CIVO rate\n    - Causal control rate\n    rows:\n    - - Walker Walk\n      - '24'\n      - ~950\n      - 2/4 (50%)\n      - 0/8 (0%)\n    - - Cheetah Run\n      - '17'\n      - ~600\n      - 3/3 (100%)\n      - 0/3 (0%)\n    - - Cartpole Swingup\n      - '5'\n      - ~860\n      - 3/3 (100%)\n      - 0/3 (0%)\n    - - Hopper Hop\n      - '15'\n      - ~280\n      - 2/3 (67%)\n      - 0/3 (0%)\n    - - '**Total**'\n      - —\n      - —\n      - '**10/13 (77%)**'\n      - '**0/17 (0%)**'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cross-environment radar chart: CIVO rate, severity, eval retention, causal control\n    effectiveness'\n  analysis: Hopper 的加入使总 CIVO detection 达 10/13（77%）和因果控制 0/17（100% prevention）。 但\n    median 档审稿人的核心攻击不在环境数量而在环境多样性： 全部 4 个都是 DMC continuous control + proprioceptive\n    observation + RSSM。 要 \"truly generalize\" 需要不同 world model（IRIS/TWM）或 pixel observation。\n    此实验在 median 档中被视为 \"nice to have\" 而非 \"changes the verdict\"。\n","numLines":1105,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1105}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VioEsxJerQ86gyAf8hfuAL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read both the PDF paper (13 pages) and the review context YAML. Let me summarize what I have:\n\n**Paper**: \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Diagnostic Analysis of Conditioning-Induced Value Overestimation in Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\nThe paper identifies CIVO (conditioning-induced value overestimation) as the primary failure mechanism when adding Δt-conditioning to DreamerV3. Key contributions:\n1. Trained Δt-embedding is necessary condition for CIVO (0/17 causal control, 10/13 CIVO trigger)\n\n\n2. NVE diagnostic metric reliably detects the problem (AUROC=0.969 across 29 experiments)\n3. Seven intervention attempts across three levels all fail to resolve it, with only marginal success in gradient-based approaches\n4. The issue is architecturally specific: model predictive control succeeds while imagination-based planning fails\n\n**Review context YAML**: Contains imagined experiments with expected results for a \"median\" tier review. The narrative guidance suggests weaknesses around statistical power, unverified assumptions, and claim strength.\n\nNow I need to dispatch two reviewers: R1 for methods and experiments, R2 for novelty and related work, then conduct a meta-review.\n\nI'll structure this as a 4-step roundtable where the reviewers first work independently, then share findings, identify convergence points, and synthesize their assessments. Let me launch both as parallel agents.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36258,"cache_read_input_tokens":23074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36258},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8160c2d3-e1f0-4475-97c0-9800d500973c","uuid":"9bfc14d3-e257-4b40-93ed-e4cf022171fc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VioEsxJerQ86gyAf8hfuAL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"论文和实验设计上下文已读取完毕。现在分派两位 Reviewer 进行独立盲审。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36258,"cache_read_input_tokens":23074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36258},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8160c2d3-e1f0-4475-97c0-9800d500973c","uuid":"196dad10-4d4f-4696-968b-45b58a7622f0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VioEsxJerQ86gyAf8hfuAL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J4CYfChd938iDu1LvALH75","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a top ML venue (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Paper summary\n\n**Title**: \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Diagnostic Analysis of Conditioning-Induced Value Overestimation in Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\nThe paper investigates why adding temporal step size Δt conditioning to DreamerV3's RSSM world model fails. It identifies \"conditioning-induced value overestimation\" (CIVO) as the primary failure mechanism: the trained Δt-embedding enables the critic to exploit imprecise multi-step RSSM predictions, creating a positive feedback loop between value overestimation and actor exploitation.\n\n## Key claims and evidence\n\n**C1**: Trained Δt-embedding is the necessary condition for CIVO. Removing it (dim=0) prevents CIVO in all 17 tested seeds (0/17 collapse) but degrades reward prediction (30–75× baseline MAE). Freezing it prevents CIVO but causes gradient starvation (eval=22% baseline). Unexposed trained embedding (subsample OFF) also prevents CIVO with 84-85% baseline retention across 2 environments.\n\n**C2**: NVE (normalized value-estimation ratio) > 1.5× is a reliable diagnostic marker. AUROC=0.969, n=29 datapoints across 4 DMC environments. Leave-one-environment-out cross-validation AUROC 0.92-0.97. Bootstrap 95% CI [0.91, 1.00]. Youden-optimal threshold converges to 1.53×.\n\n**C3**: Seven intervention methods across three levels fail to reliably mitigate CIVO:\n- L1 Gradient (SGS): 1/17 success. Reward-only SGS is no-op (NVE=10.42×). Full SGS 0/3. Obs-decoder SGS 1/6.\n- L2 Output (RAVE): 0/2. EMA anchor polluted by CIVO-biased values.\n- L3 Representation (TCN): 2/8. Walker σ=0.2 works 2/3 seeds but fails on Cheetah. σ=1.0 prevents CIVO but kills learning.\n\n**C4**: MPC vs imagination architectural dependency. TAWM (MPC-based) succeeds with Δt-conditioning while DreamerV3 (imagination-based AC) fails. Presented as \"empirical observation consistent with architectural dependency\" not a causal claim.\n\n## Experimental design\n\n- **Environments**: 4 DMC tasks (Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup, Hopper Hop), obs dim 5-24\n- **Factorial grid**: 3 factors (Δt-embedding status × temporal subsampling × imagination horizon)\n- **Seeds**: 2-4 per configuration (typically 3)\n- **Training**: 105K-200K steps\n- **Key configs**: 008d (trained dt_emb, CIVO trigger), 008f (dim=0, causal control), 008a (unexposed, V-recovery), 008e_v3 (dt=1 imagination), 015b (frozen), plus intervention variants\n\n## Key tables from the paper\n\nTable 1 (Cross-environment CIVO summary):\n| Environment | Obs dim | Baseline | CIVO rate | Causal control |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Walker Walk | 24 | ~950 | 2/4 (50%) | 0/8 (0%) |\n| Cheetah Run | 17 | ~600 | 3/3 (100%) | 0/3 (0%) |\n| Cartpole Swingup | 5 | ~860 | 3/3 (100%) | 0/3 (0%) |\n| Hopper Hop | 15 | ~280 | 2/3 (67%) | 0/3 (0%) |\n| **Total** | — | — | **10/13 (77%)** | **0/17 (0%)** |\n\nTable 5 (Δt-embedding ablation matrix, Walker Walk):\n| | Exposed (Δt>1) | Unexposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Trained | 008d: CIVO (NVE 2.09×) | 008a: V-recovery (NVE 0.59×) |\n| Frozen | 015b: gradient starvation (NVE 0.42×) | (equivalent to 008a, cancelled) |\n| Removed | 008f: reward degradation (NVE 0.30×) | N/A |\n\nTable 8 (NVE threshold sensitivity):\n| Threshold | Sensitivity | Specificity | Accuracy | Youden J |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.3× | 0.94 | 0.80 | 0.86 | 0.74 |\n| 1.5× | 0.88 | 1.00 | 0.93 | 0.88 |\n| 1.53× (optimal) | 0.88 | 1.00 | 0.93 | 0.88 |\n\nTable 11 (008e_v3, dt=1 imagination, 4 seeds):\n| Seed | Eval@105K | NVE peak | Collapse? | Pathway |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| s1 | 870 | 0.80 | No | — |\n| s2 | 137 | 3.78 | Yes | B (IRD, entropy ↑) |\n| s3 | 93 | 4.02 | Yes | A-like (entropy ↓) |\n| s4 | 899 | 0.99 | No | — |\n| Rate | — | — | 2/4=50% | Mixed |\n\nTable 14 (RSSM fidelity):\n| Model | Δt1 obs MSE | Δt2 obs MSE | Obs gap | Δt1 rew MAE | Δt2 rew MAE | Rew gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Baseline | 13.49 | 27.50 | 2.04× | 0.0102 | 0.0159 | 1.56× |\n| 008d (trained) | 41.31 | 53.67 | 1.30× | 0.0568 | 0.1579 | 2.78× |\n| 008f (no emb) | 8.01 | 22.04 | 2.75× | 0.7469 | 0.7526 | 1.01× |\n\nTable 15 (Intervention hierarchy):\n| Level | Method | Success rate | Seeds | Failure mechanism |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| L1: Gradient | Full SGS | 0/3 | 3 | Forward-pass damage irreversible |\n| L1: Gradient | Obs-decoder SGS | 1/6 | 6 | Compensatory amplification |\n| L1: Gradient | Reward SGS | 0/2 | 2 | No-op (gradient ≠ causality) |\n| L2: Output | RAVE ceil=2.0 | 0/1 | 1 | EMA anchor polluted |\n| L2: Output | RAVE ceil=1.5 | 0/1 | 1 | EMA anchor polluted |\n| L3: Repr. | TCN σ=0.2 | 2/3 | 3 | Walker-only; s2 CIVO@95K |\n| L3: Repr. | TCN σ=0.5 | 0/3 | 3 | Overdose / still insufficient |\n| L4: Model | Unc. truncation | 0/1 | 1 | Effective horizon reduction |\n| Control | Δt-emb removal | 5/5 | 5 | (Not an intervention) |\n\n## Experiment design reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe imagined experiment list includes these experiments that may or may not be fully reflected in the paper:\n1. Walker Walk 008d seeds 1-2 (CIVO collapse cross-seed reproducibility) — in paper ✓\n2. Walker Walk 008f seeds 1-2 (dt_embed_dim=0 stability) — in paper ✓ \n3. Walker Walk 008e_v3 seeds 1-2 (mitigation partially falsified) — in paper ✓\n4. Walker Walk 008a seeds 1-2 (unexposed dt_emb V-recovery) — in paper ✓\n5. Walker Walk 008e_v3 seeds 3-4 (expand CI) — in paper ✓\n6. Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb (015b) — in paper ✓\n7. Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds) — in paper ✓\n8. Cheetah Run CIVO trigger (3 seeds) — in paper (partially, 2 seeds confirmed + 1 predicted as ~85)\n9. Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 (3 seeds) — in paper (partially, 2 seeds confirmed)\n10. Cheetah Run unexposed dt_emb (3 seeds) — in paper (partially, 2 seeds confirmed)\n11. RSSM prediction quality analysis — in paper ✓\n12. Actor entropy analysis — in paper ✓\n13. NVE threshold sensitivity + AUROC — in paper ✓\n14. Cartpole Swingup baseline — in paper ✓\n15. Cartpole Swingup CIVO trigger — in paper ✓\n16. Cartpole Swingup causal control — in paper ✓\n17. Uncertainty-gated truncation pilot — in paper ✓\n18. Hopper Hop validation — in paper ✓ (mentioned in tables, limited detail)\n19. Value prediction distribution analysis — NOT clearly in paper\n20. dt_embedding cosine similarity — NOT clearly in paper\n\n## Your task\n\nWrite a detailed review focusing on **Methods and Experiments**. Evaluate:\n\n1. **Experimental design quality**: Is the factorial design appropriate? Are controls adequate? Are there confounds?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Are the seed counts sufficient? Are confidence intervals and statistical tests appropriate? Is the AUROC analysis valid given n=29 and in-sample calibration?\n3. **Reproducibility**: Are enough details provided to reproduce? Are hyperparameters specified?\n4. **Completeness**: Are there obvious experiments missing? Does the intervention hierarchy cover the right space? Should standard overestimation countermeasures (Double Q, ensemble critics) have been tried?\n5. **Claim-evidence alignment**: Do the experiments actually support the claims made? Are claims appropriately scoped?\n\nStructure your review as:\n- **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n- **Strengths** (numbered list with brief explanations)\n- **Weaknesses** (numbered list, labeled Major/Minor, with specific suggestions)\n- **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n- **Missing Experiments** (what should have been included)\n- **Scores**: Soundness (1-4), Contribution (1-4), Clarity (1-4), Overall (1-6), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a diagnostic/negative-result paper — judge it by diagnostic standards, not by whether it proposes a solution.","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36258,"cache_read_input_tokens":23074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36258},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8160c2d3-e1f0-4475-97c0-9800d500973c","uuid":"f6b48d52-da8e-4d7f-92c7-7403734d7901"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a3e85d58564f5b039","tool_use_id":"toolu_01J4CYfChd938iDu1LvALH75","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a top ML venue (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Paper summary\n\n**Title**: \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Diagnostic Analysis of Conditioning-Induced Value Overestimation in Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\nThe paper investigates why adding temporal step size Δt conditioning to DreamerV3's RSSM world model fails. It identifies \"conditioning-induced value overestimation\" (CIVO) as the primary failure mechanism: the trained Δt-embedding enables the critic to exploit imprecise multi-step RSSM predictions, creating a positive feedback loop between value overestimation and actor exploitation.\n\n## Key claims and evidence\n\n**C1**: Trained Δt-embedding is the necessary condition for CIVO. Removing it (dim=0) prevents CIVO in all 17 tested seeds (0/17 collapse) but degrades reward prediction (30–75× baseline MAE). Freezing it prevents CIVO but causes gradient starvation (eval=22% baseline). Unexposed trained embedding (subsample OFF) also prevents CIVO with 84-85% baseline retention across 2 environments.\n\n**C2**: NVE (normalized value-estimation ratio) > 1.5× is a reliable diagnostic marker. AUROC=0.969, n=29 datapoints across 4 DMC environments. Leave-one-environment-out cross-validation AUROC 0.92-0.97. Bootstrap 95% CI [0.91, 1.00]. Youden-optimal threshold converges to 1.53×.\n\n**C3**: Seven intervention methods across three levels fail to reliably mitigate CIVO:\n- L1 Gradient (SGS): 1/17 success. Reward-only SGS is no-op (NVE=10.42×). Full SGS 0/3. Obs-decoder SGS 1/6.\n- L2 Output (RAVE): 0/2. EMA anchor polluted by CIVO-biased values.\n- L3 Representation (TCN): 2/8. Walker σ=0.2 works 2/3 seeds but fails on Cheetah. σ=1.0 prevents CIVO but kills learning.\n\n**C4**: MPC vs imagination architectural dependency. TAWM (MPC-based) succeeds with Δt-conditioning while DreamerV3 (imagination-based AC) fails. Presented as \"empirical observation consistent with architectural dependency\" not a causal claim.\n\n## Experimental design\n\n- **Environments**: 4 DMC tasks (Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup, Hopper Hop), obs dim 5-24\n- **Factorial grid**: 3 factors (Δt-embedding status × temporal subsampling × imagination horizon)\n- **Seeds**: 2-4 per configuration (typically 3)\n- **Training**: 105K-200K steps\n- **Key configs**: 008d (trained dt_emb, CIVO trigger), 008f (dim=0, causal control), 008a (unexposed, V-recovery), 008e_v3 (dt=1 imagination), 015b (frozen), plus intervention variants\n\n## Key tables from the paper\n\nTable 1 (Cross-environment CIVO summary):\n| Environment | Obs dim | Baseline | CIVO rate | Causal control |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Walker Walk | 24 | ~950 | 2/4 (50%) | 0/8 (0%) |\n| Cheetah Run | 17 | ~600 | 3/3 (100%) | 0/3 (0%) |\n| Cartpole Swingup | 5 | ~860 | 3/3 (100%) | 0/3 (0%) |\n| Hopper Hop | 15 | ~280 | 2/3 (67%) | 0/3 (0%) |\n| **Total** | — | — | **10/13 (77%)** | **0/17 (0%)** |\n\nTable 5 (Δt-embedding ablation matrix, Walker Walk):\n| | Exposed (Δt>1) | Unexposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Trained | 008d: CIVO (NVE 2.09×) | 008a: V-recovery (NVE 0.59×) |\n| Frozen | 015b: gradient starvation (NVE 0.42×) | (equivalent to 008a, cancelled) |\n| Removed | 008f: reward degradation (NVE 0.30×) | N/A |\n\nTable 8 (NVE threshold sensitivity):\n| Threshold | Sensitivity | Specificity | Accuracy | Youden J |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.3× | 0.94 | 0.80 | 0.86 | 0.74 |\n| 1.5× | 0.88 | 1.00 | 0.93 | 0.88 |\n| 1.53× (optimal) | 0.88 | 1.00 | 0.93 | 0.88 |\n\nTable 11 (008e_v3, dt=1 imagination, 4 seeds):\n| Seed | Eval@105K | NVE peak | Collapse? | Pathway |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| s1 | 870 | 0.80 | No | — |\n| s2 | 137 | 3.78 | Yes | B (IRD, entropy ↑) |\n| s3 | 93 | 4.02 | Yes | A-like (entropy ↓) |\n| s4 | 899 | 0.99 | No | — |\n| Rate | — | — | 2/4=50% | Mixed |\n\nTable 14 (RSSM fidelity):\n| Model | Δt1 obs MSE | Δt2 obs MSE | Obs gap | Δt1 rew MAE | Δt2 rew MAE | Rew gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Baseline | 13.49 | 27.50 | 2.04× | 0.0102 | 0.0159 | 1.56× |\n| 008d (trained) | 41.31 | 53.67 | 1.30× | 0.0568 | 0.1579 | 2.78× |\n| 008f (no emb) | 8.01 | 22.04 | 2.75× | 0.7469 | 0.7526 | 1.01× |\n\nTable 15 (Intervention hierarchy):\n| Level | Method | Success rate | Seeds | Failure mechanism |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| L1: Gradient | Full SGS | 0/3 | 3 | Forward-pass damage irreversible |\n| L1: Gradient | Obs-decoder SGS | 1/6 | 6 | Compensatory amplification |\n| L1: Gradient | Reward SGS | 0/2 | 2 | No-op (gradient ≠ causality) |\n| L2: Output | RAVE ceil=2.0 | 0/1 | 1 | EMA anchor polluted |\n| L2: Output | RAVE ceil=1.5 | 0/1 | 1 | EMA anchor polluted |\n| L3: Repr. | TCN σ=0.2 | 2/3 | 3 | Walker-only; s2 CIVO@95K |\n| L3: Repr. | TCN σ=0.5 | 0/3 | 3 | Overdose / still insufficient |\n| L4: Model | Unc. truncation | 0/1 | 1 | Effective horizon reduction |\n| Control | Δt-emb removal | 5/5 | 5 | (Not an intervention) |\n\n## Experiment design reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe imagined experiment list includes these experiments that may or may not be fully reflected in the paper:\n1. Walker Walk 008d seeds 1-2 (CIVO collapse cross-seed reproducibility) — in paper ✓\n2. Walker Walk 008f seeds 1-2 (dt_embed_dim=0 stability) — in paper ✓ \n3. Walker Walk 008e_v3 seeds 1-2 (mitigation partially falsified) — in paper ✓\n4. Walker Walk 008a seeds 1-2 (unexposed dt_emb V-recovery) — in paper ✓\n5. Walker Walk 008e_v3 seeds 3-4 (expand CI) — in paper ✓\n6. Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb (015b) — in paper ✓\n7. Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds) — in paper ✓\n8. Cheetah Run CIVO trigger (3 seeds) — in paper (partially, 2 seeds confirmed + 1 predicted as ~85)\n9. Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 (3 seeds) — in paper (partially, 2 seeds confirmed)\n10. Cheetah Run unexposed dt_emb (3 seeds) — in paper (partially, 2 seeds confirmed)\n11. RSSM prediction quality analysis — in paper ✓\n12. Actor entropy analysis — in paper ✓\n13. NVE threshold sensitivity + AUROC — in paper ✓\n14. Cartpole Swingup baseline — in paper ✓\n15. Cartpole Swingup CIVO trigger — in paper ✓\n16. Cartpole Swingup causal control — in paper ✓\n17. Uncertainty-gated truncation pilot — in paper ✓\n18. Hopper Hop validation — in paper ✓ (mentioned in tables, limited detail)\n19. Value prediction distribution analysis — NOT clearly in paper\n20. dt_embedding cosine similarity — NOT clearly in paper\n\n## Your task\n\nWrite a detailed review focusing on **Methods and Experiments**. Evaluate:\n\n1. **Experimental design quality**: Is the factorial design appropriate? Are controls adequate? Are there confounds?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Are the seed counts sufficient? Are confidence intervals and statistical tests appropriate? Is the AUROC analysis valid given n=29 and in-sample calibration?\n3. **Reproducibility**: Are enough details provided to reproduce? Are hyperparameters specified?\n4. **Completeness**: Are there obvious experiments missing? Does the intervention hierarchy cover the right space? Should standard overestimation countermeasures (Double Q, ensemble critics) have been tried?\n5. **Claim-evidence alignment**: Do the experiments actually support the claims made? Are claims appropriately scoped?\n\nStructure your review as:\n- **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n- **Strengths** (numbered list with brief explanations)\n- **Weaknesses** (numbered list, labeled Major/Minor, with specific suggestions)\n- **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n- **Missing Experiments** (what should have been included)\n- **Scores**: Soundness (1-4), Contribution (1-4), Clarity (1-4), Overall (1-6), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a diagnostic/negative-result paper — judge it by diagnostic standards, not by whether it proposes a solution.","uuid":"efe504cf-a628-499d-b0d9-922b022db141","session_id":"8160c2d3-e1f0-4475-97c0-9800d500973c"}
